\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 The conception of God and the conception of Absolute Truth are not on the same level. The }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 hits on the target of the Absolute Truth. The conception of God indicates the controller, whereas the conception of the Absolute Truth indicates the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
summum bonum }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
the ultimate source of all energies. There is no difference of opinion about the personal feature of God as the controller because a controller cannot be impersonal. Of course modern government, especially democratic government, is imperso
nal to some extent, but ultimately the chief executive head is a person, and the impersonal feature of government is subordinate to the personal feature. So without a doubt whenever we refer to control over others we must admit the existence of a personal
 feature. Because there are different controllers for different managerial positions, there may be many small gods. According to the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
any controller who has some specific extraordinary power is called a }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 vibh\'fctimat sattva, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or controller empowered by the Lord. There are many }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 vibh\'fctimat sattvas, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 controllers or gods with various specific powers, but the Absolute Truth is one without a second. This }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 designates the Absolute Truth or the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 summum bonum }{
