\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 A SHORT SKETCH OF THE LIFE AND TEACHINGS OF LORD CAITANYA, THE PREACHER OF \'c7R\'c9MAD-BH\'c4GAVATAM 
\par }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Lord \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu, the great apostle of love of God and the father of the congregational chanting of the holy name of the Lord, advented Himself at \'c7r\'e9dh\'e4ma M\'e4y\'e4
pura, a quarter in the city of Navadv\'e9pa in Bengal, on the }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723 Ph\'e4lguni}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  P\'fcr\'ebim\'e4 evening in the year 1407 }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7ak}{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723 a}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 bda }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 (corresponding to February 1486 by the Christian calendar).
\par His father, \'c7r\'e9 Jagann\'e4tha Mi\'e7ra, a learned }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'eba }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 from the district of Sylhet, came to Navadv\'e9
pa as a student because at that time Navadv\'e9pa was considered to be the center of education and culture. He domiciled on the banks of the Ganges after marrying \'c7r\'e9mat\'e9 \'c7ac\'e9dev\'e9, a daughter of \'c7r\'e9la N\'e9l\'e4mbara Cakravart\'e9
, the great learned scholar of Navadv\'e9pa.
\par Jagann\'e4tha Mi\'e7ra had a number of daughters by his wife \'c7r\'e9mat\'e9 \'c7ac\'e9dev\'e9, and most of them expired at an early age. Two surviving sons, \'c7r\'e9 Vi\'e7var\'fcpa and Vi\'e7
vambhara, became at last the object of their paternal affection. The tenth and youngest son, who was named Vi\'e7vambhara, later became known as Nim\'e4i Pa\'eb\'f2it and then, after accepting the renounced order of life, Lord \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4p
rabhu.
\par Lord \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu exhibited His transcendental activities for forty-eight years and then disappeared in the year 1455 }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723\charrsid14297723 \'c7akabda}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 at Pur\'e9.
\par For His first twenty-four years He remained at Navadv\'e9pa as a student and householder. His first wife was \'c7r\'e9mat\'e9 Lak\'f1m\'e9priy\'e4
, who died at an early age when the Lord was away from home. When He returned from East Bengal He was requested by His mother to accept a second wife, and He agreed. His second wife was \'c7r\'e9mat\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebupriy\'e4 Dev\'e9
, who bore the separation of the Lord throughout her life because the Lord took the order of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4sa }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 at the age of twenty-four when \'c7r\'e9mat\'e9 Vi
\'f1\'ebupriy\'e4 was barely sixteen years old.
\par After taking }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4sa, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 the Lord made His headquarters at Jagann\'e4tha Pur\'e9 due to the request of His mother, \'c7r\'e9mat\'e9 \'c7ac\'e9dev\'e9
 The Lord remained for twenty-four years at Pur\'e9. For six years of this time He travelled continuously all over India (and especially throughout southern India) preaching the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam.

\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Lord Caitanya not only preached the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 but propagated the teaching of the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 as well in the most practical way. In the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba is depicted as the Absolute Personality of Godhead, and His last teaching
s in that great book of transcendental knowledge instruct that one should give up all the modes of religious activities and accept Him (Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba) as the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 only worshipable }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Lord. The Lord then assured that all His devotees would be protected from all sorts of sinful acts and that for them there would be no cause for anxiety.
\par Unfortunately, despite Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba's direct order and the teachings of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
less intelligent people misunderstand Him to be nothing but a great historical personalit
y, and thus they cannot accept Him as the original Personality of Godhead. Such men with a poor fund of knowledge are misled by many nondevotees. Thus the teachings of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 were misinterpreted even by great scholars. After the disappearance of Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba there were hundreds of commentaries on the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t
\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 by many erudite scholars, and almost every one of them was motivated by self-interest.
\par Lord \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu is the selfsame Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba. This time, however, He appeared as 
a great devotee of the Lord in order to preach to the people in general, as well as to religionists and philosophers, about the transcendental position of \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, the primeval Lord and the cause of all causes. The essence of His preaching is that Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba, who appeared at Vrajabh\'fcmi (V\'e5nd\'e4vana) as the son of the King of Vraja (Nanda Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja), is the Supreme Personality of Godhead and is therefore worshipable by all. V\'e5nd\'e4vana-dh\'e4ma is nondifferent from the Lord because the name, fame, form and pla
ce where the Lord manifests Himself are all identical with the Lord as absolute knowledge. Therefore V\'e5nd\'e4vana-dh\'e4ma is as worshipable as the Lord. The highest form of transcendental worship of the Lord was exhibited by the damsels of Vrajabh\'fc
mi in the form of pure affection for the Lord, and Lord \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu recommends this process as the most excellent mode of worship. He accepts the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavata Pur\'e4\'eb
a }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 as the spotless literature for understanding the Lord, and He preached that the ultimate goal of life for all human beings is to attain the stage of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 prem
\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or love of God.
