was a champion scholar, and he had travelled to all places of learning in India. Finally he came to Navadv\'e9pa to contest the learned }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 pa\'eb\'f2its }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
there. The }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 pa\'eb\'f2its }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 of Navadv\'e9pa decided to match Nim\'e4i Pa\'eb\'f2it (Lord Caitanya) with the Kashmir Pa\'eb\'f2it, thinking that if Nim\'e4i Pa
\'eb\'f2it were defeated, they would have another chance to debate with the scholar, for Nim\'e4i Pa\'eb\'f2it was only a boy. And if the Kashmir Pa\'eb\'f2
