\par The Lord was then married with great pomp and gaiety, and at this time He began to preach the congregational chanting of the holy name of the Lord at Navadv\'e9pa. Some of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'ebas }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 became envious of His popularity, and they put many hindrances on His path. They were so jealous that they finally took the matter before the Muslim magistrate at Navadv\'e9pa. Bengal was then governed by Pa
thans, and the governor of the province was Nawab Hussain Shah. The Muslim magistrate of Navadv\'e9pa took up the complaints of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'ebas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
seriously, and at first he warned the followers of Nim\'e4i Pa\'eb\'f2it not to chant loudly the name of Hari. But Lord Caitanya asked His followers to disobey the orders of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Kazi, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and they went on with their }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
(chanting) party as usual. The magistrate then sent constables who interrupted a }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and broke some of the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 m\'e5da\'ecgas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 (drums). When Nim\'e4i Pa\'eb\'f2
it heard of this incidence He organized a party for civil disobedience. He is the pioneer of the civil disobedience movement in India for the right cause. He organized a procession of 100,000 men with thousands of }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 m\'e5da\'ecgas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 karat\'e4las }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 (hand cymbals), and
 this procession passed over the roads of Navadv\'e9pa in defiance of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Kazi }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 who issued the order. Finally the procession reached the house of the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Kazi, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 who went upstairs out of fear of the masses. The great crowds assembled at the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Kazi's }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 house displayed a violent temper, but the Lord asked them to be peaceful. At this time the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Kazi }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
came down and tried to pacify the Lord by addressing Him as his nephew. He pointed out that N\'e9l\'e4mbara Cakravart\'e9 referred to him as an uncle, and consequently, \'c7r\'e9mat\'e9 \'c7ac\'e9dev\'e9, the mother of Nim\'e4i Pa\'eb\'f2
it, was his sister. He asked the Lord whether his sister's son could be angry at His maternal uncle, and the Lord replied that since the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Kazi }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
was His maternal uncle he should receive his nephew well at his home. In this way the issue was mitigated, and the two learned scholars began a long discussion on the Koran and Hindu}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  \'e7\'e4stras. }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 The Lord raised the question of cow killing, and the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Kazi }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
properly answered Him by referring to the Koran. In turn the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Kazi }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 also questioned the Lord about cow sacrifice in the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and the Lord replied that such sacrifice as mentioned in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is not actually cow killing. In that sacrifice an old bull or cow was sacrificed for the sake of receiving a fresh younger life by the power of Vedic }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 mantras. 
}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 But in the Kali-yuga such cow sacrifices are forbidden because there are no qualified }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'ebas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
capable of conducting such a sacrifice. In fact, in Kali-yuga all }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 yaj\'efas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
(sacrifices) are forbidden because they are useless attempts by foolish men. In Kali-yuga only the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana yaj\'efa }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
is recommended for all practical purposes. Speaking in this way, the Lord finally convinced the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Kazi, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 who became the Lord's follower. The }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Kazi }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 thenceforth declared that no one should hinder the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 movement which was started by the Lord, and the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Kazi }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 left this order in his will for the sake of progeny. The }
{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Kazi's }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 tomb still exists in the area of Navadv\'e9pa, and Hindu pilgrims go there to show their respects. The }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Kazi's }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 descendants are residents, and they never objected to }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 even during the Hindu Muslim riot days.
\par This incidence shows clearly that the Lord was not a so-called timid Vai\'f1\'ebava. A Vai\'f1\'ebava is a fearless devotee of the Lord, and for the right cause he can take any step suitable for the purpose. Arjuna was also a Vai\'f1\'eb
ava devotee of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and he fought valiantly for the satisfaction of the Lord. Similarly, Vajr\'e4\'ecgaj\'e9, or Hanum\'e4n, was also a devotee of Lord R\'e4ma, and he gave lessons to the nondevotee party of R\'e4va\'eb
a. The principles of Vai\'f1\'ebavism are to satisfy the Lord by all means. A Vai\'f1\'ebava is by nature a nonviolent, peaceful living being, and he has all the good qualities of God, but when the nondevotee blasphemes the Lord or His devotee, the Vai
\'f1\'ebava never tolerates such impudency.
\par After this incidence the Lord began to preach and propagate His }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 movement, more vigorously, and whoever stood against this propagation of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 yuga-dharma, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
or duty of the age, was properly punished by various types of chastisement. Two }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'eba }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 gentlemen named Chapala and Gop\'e4
la, who also happened to be maternal uncles of the Lord, were inflicted with leprosy by way of chastisement, and later, when they were repentant, they were accepted by the Lord. In the course of His preaching work, He us
ed to send daily all His followers, including \'c7r\'e9la Nity\'e4nanda Prabhu and \'d6h\'e4kur Harid\'e4sa, two chief whips of His party, from door to door to preach the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam. }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 All of Navadv\'e9pa was surcharged with His }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 movement, and His head quarters 
were situated at the house of \'c7r\'e9v\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kur and \'c7r\'e9 Advaita Prabhu, two of His chief householder disciples. These two learned heads of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'eba }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 community were the most ardent supporters of Lord Caitanya's movement. \'c7r\'e9 Advaita Prabhu was the chief cau
se for the advent of the Lord. When Advaita Prabhu saw that the total human society was full of materialistic activities and devoid of devotional service, which alone could save mankind from the threefold miseries of material existence, he, out of his cau
seless compassion for the age-worn human society, prayed fervently for the incarnation of the Lord and continually worshiped the Lord with the water of the Ganges and the leaves of the holy }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 tulas\'e9 }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 tree. As far as preaching work in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 movement wa
s concerned, everyone was expected to do his daily share according to the order of the Lord.
\par Once Nity\'e4nanda Prabhu and \'c7r\'e9la Harid\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kur were walking down a main road, and on the way they saw a roaring crowd assembled. Upon inquiring}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid934474  }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
from passers-by, they understood that two brothers, named }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid934474 Jagai}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  and }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid934474 Madhai}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
, were creating a public disturbance in a drunken state. They also heard that these two brothers were born in a respectable }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'eba }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
family, but because of low association they had turned into debauchees of the worst type. They were not only drunkards but also meat-eaters, woman-hunters, decoits and sinners of all description. \'c7r\'e9la Nity\'e4
nanda Prabhu heard all of these stories and decided that these two fallen souls must be the first to be delivered. 
If they were delivered from their sinful life, then the good name of Lord Caitanya would be even still more glorified. Thinking in this way, Nity\'e4nanda Prabhu and Harid\'e4
sa pushed their way through the crowd and asked the two brothers to chant the holy name of Lord Hari. The drunken brothers became enraged upon this request and attacked Nity\'e4
nanda Prabhu with filthy language. Both brothers chased them a considerable distance. In the evening the report of the preaching work was submitted to the Lord, and He was glad to learn that Nity\'e4nanda and Harid\'e4
sa had attempted to deliver such a stupid pair of fellows.
\par The next day Nity\'e4nanda Prabhu went to see the brothers, and as soon as He approached them one of them threw a piece of earthen pot at Him. This struck Him on the forehead, and immediately blood began to flow. But Nity\'e4
nanda Prabhu was so kind that instead of protesting this heinous act, He said, "It does not matter that you have thrown this stone at Me. I still request you to chant the holy name of Lord Hari."
\par One of the brothers, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid934474 Jagai}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 , was astonished to see this behavior of Nity\'e4nanda Prabhu, and he at once fell down at His feet and asked Him to pardon his sinful brother. When }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid934474 Madhai}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  again attempted to hurt Nity\'e4nanda Prabhu, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid934474 Jagai}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
 stopped him and implored him to fall down at His feet.
\par In the meantime the news of Nity\'e4nanda's injury reached the Lord, who at once hurried to the spot in a fiery and angry mood. The Lord immediately invoked His Sudar\'e7ana-cakra (the Lord's ultimate weapo
n, shaped like a wheel) to kill the sinners, but Nity\'e4nanda Prabhu reminded Him of His mission. The mission of the Lord was to deliver the hopelessly fallen souls of Kali-yuga, and the brothers }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid934474 Jagai}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  and }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid934474 Madhai}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  were typical examples of these fallen souls. 
Ninety percent of the population of this age resembles these brothers, despite }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid934474 high birth and mundane respecta}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
bility. According to the verdict of the revealed scriptures, the total population of the world in this age will be of the lowest }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7\'fcdra }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 quality, or
 even lower. It should be noted that \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu never acknowledged the stereotyped caste system by birthright; rather, He strictly followed the verdict of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7\'e4stras }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 in the matter of one's }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid934474 s}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 var\'fcpa, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or real identity.
\par When the Lord was invoking His Sudar\'e7ana-cakra and \'c7r\'e9la Nity\'e4
nanda Prabhu was imploring Him to forgive the two brothers, both the brothers fell down at the lotus feet of the Lord and begged His pardon for their gross behavior. The Lord was also asked by Nity\'e4nanda Prabhu to accept
 these repenting souls, and the Lord agreed to accept them on one condition, that they henceforward completely give up all their sinful activities and habits of debauchery. Both the brothers agreed and promised to give up all their sinful habits, and the 
kind Lord accepted them and did not again refer to their past misdeeds.
\par This is the specific kindness of Lord Caitanya. In this age no one can say that he is free from sin. It is impossible for anyone to say this. But Lord Caitanya accepts all kinds of sinf
ul persons on the one condition that they promise not to indulge in sinful habits after being spiritually initiated by the bona fide spiritual master.
\par There are a number of instructive points to be observed in this incidence of the two brothers. In this Kali-yuga practically all people are of the quality of }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid934474 Jagai}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  and }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid934474 Madhai}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 . If they want to be relieved from the reactions of their misdeeds, they must take shelter of Lord Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu and after spiritual initiation thus refrain from those things which are prohibited in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7\'e4stras. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
The prohibitory rules are dealt with in the Lord's teachings to \'c7r\'e9la R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9.
\par During His householder life, the Lord did not display many of the miracles which are generally expected from such personalities, but He did once perform a wonderful miracle in the house of \'c7r\'e9niv\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kur while }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 was in full swing. He asked the devotees what they wanted to eat, and when He was informed that they
 wanted to eat mangos, He asked for a seed of a mango, although this fruit was out of season. When the seed was brought to Him He sowed it in the yard of \'c7r\'e9niv\'e4
sa, and at once a creeper began to grow out of the seed. Within no time this creeper became a full-grown mango tree heavy with more ripened fruits than the devotees could eat. The tree remained in \'c7r\'e9niv\'e4
sa's yard, and from then on the devotees used to take as many mangos from the tree as they wanted.
\par The Lord had a very high estimation of the affections of the damsels of Vrajabh\'fcmi (V\'e5nd\'e4vana) for K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and in appreciation of their unalloyed service to the Lord, once \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu chanted the holy names of the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 gop\'e9s }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 (cowherd girls) instead of the names of the Lord. At this time some of Hi
s students, who were also disciples, came to see Him, and when they saw that the Lord was chanting the names of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 gop\'e9s, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
they were astonished. Out of sheer foolishness they asked the Lord why He was chanting the names of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 gop\'e9s}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  and advised Him to chant the name of K\'e5
\'f1\'eba. The Lord, who was in ecstasy, was thus disturbed by these foolish students. He chastised them and chased them away. The students were almost the same age as the Lord, and thus they wrongly thought of the Lord as one of their peers. The
y held a meeting and resolved that they would attack the Lord if He dared to punish them again in such a manner. This incidence provoked some malicious talks about the Lord on the part of the general public.
\par When the Lord became aware of this, He began to consider the various types of men which are found in society. He noted that especially the students, professors, fruitive workers, }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 yog\'e9s, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 nondevotees, and different types of atheists were all opposed to the devotional service of the Lord. "My mission is to
 deliver all the fallen souls of this age," He thought, "but if they commit offenses against Me, thinking Me to be an ordinary man, they will not benefit. If they are to begin their life of spiritual realization, they must some way or another offer obeisa
nces unto Me." Thus the Lord decided to accept the renounced order of life }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 (sanny\'e4sa) }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 because people in general were inclined to offer respects to a }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9.
\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Five hundred years ago the condition of society was not as degraded as it is today. At that time people would show respects to a }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 was rigid in following the rules and regulations of the renounced order of life. \'c7r
\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu was not very much in favor of the renounced order of life in this age of Kali, but that was only for the reason that very few }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9s }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 in this age are able }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid934474 to observe the rules and regula}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 tions of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4sa }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 life. \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu decided to accept the order and become an ideal }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
so that the general populace would show Him respect. One is duty-bound to show respect to a }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 for a }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is considered to be the master of all }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 var\'ebas }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e4\'e7ramas.}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
\par While He was contemplating accepting the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4sa }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 order, it so happened that Ke\'e7ava Bh\'e4rat\'e9, a }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
sanny\'e4s\'e9 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 of the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 school and resident of Katwa (in Bengal), visited Navadv\'e9pa and was invited to dine with the Lord. When Ke\'e7ava Bh\'e4rat\'e9
 came to His house, the Lord asked him to award Him the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4sa }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 order of life. This was a matter of formality. A }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4sa }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 order is to be accepted from another }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9. }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Although the Lord was independent in all respects, still, to keep up the formalities of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7\'e4stras, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
He accepted the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4sa }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 order from Ke\'e7ava Bh\'e4rat\'e9, although Ke\'e7ava Bh\'e4rat\'e9 was not in the Vai\'f1\'ebava }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 samprad\'e4ya }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 (school).
\par After consulting with Ke\'e7ava Bh\'e4rat\'e9, the Lord left Navadv\'e9pa for Katwa to formally accept the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4sa }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 order of life. He was accompanied by 
\'c7r\'e9la Nity\'e4nanda Prabhu, Candra\'e7ekhara \'c4c\'e4rya, and Mukunda Datta. These three assisted Him in the details of the ceremony. The incidence of the Lord's accepting the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4sa }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 order is very elaborately described in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid16143250\charrsid16143250 Caitanya-bh\'e4gavata}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 by \'c7r\'e9la V\'e5nd\'e4vana-d\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kur.
\par Thus at the end of His twenty-fourth year the Lord accepted the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4sa }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 order of life in the month of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 M
\'e4gha. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 After accepting this order He became a full-fledged preacher of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
Although He was doing the same preaching work in His householder life, when He experienced some obstacles to His preaching, He sacrificed even the comfort of His h
ome life for the sake of the fallen souls. In His householder life His chief assistants were \'c7r\'e9la Advaita Prabhu and \'c7r\'e9la \'c7r\'e9v\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kur, but after He accepted the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4sa 
}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 order His chief assistants became \'c7r\'e9la Nity\'e4nanda Prabhu, who was deputed to preach specifically in Bengal, and the six Gosv\'e4m\'e9s (R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9, San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9, J\'e9
va Gosv\'e4m\'e9, Gop\'e4la Bha\'f6\'f6a Gosv\'e4m\'e9, Raghun\'e4tha D\'e4sa Gosv\'e4m\'e9, and Raghun\'e4tha Bha\'f6\'f6a Gosv\'e4m\'e9), headed by \'c7r\'e9la R\'fcpa and San\'e4tana, who were deputed to go to V\'e5nd\'e4vana to excava
te the present places of pilgrimage. The present city of V\'e5nd\'e4vana and the importance of Vrajabh\'fcmi were thus disclosed by the will of Lord \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu.
\par The Lord, after accepting the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4sa }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 order, at once wanted to start for V\'e5nd\'e4vana. For th
ree continual days He travelled in the Radha Desha (places where the Ganges does not flow). He was in full ecstasy over the idea of going to V\'e5nd\'e4vana. However, \'c7r\'e9la Nity\'e4
nanda Prabhu diverted His path and brought Him instead to the house of Advaita Prabhu in }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1007972\charrsid12326592 \'c7\'e4}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ntipura. The Lord stayed at \'c7r\'e9
 Advaita Prabhu's house for a few days, and knowing well that the Lord was leaving His hearth and home for good, \'c7r\'e9 Advaita Prabhu sent his men to Navadv\'e9pa to bring mother \'c7ac\'e9 to have a last meeting with her son. So
me unscrupulous people say that Lord Caitanya met His wife also after taking }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4sa }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
and offered her His wooden slipper for worship, but the authentic sources give no information about such a meeting. His mother met Him at the house of Advaita Prabhu, and when she saw her son in }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4
sa, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 she lamented. By way of compromise, she requested her son to make His headquarters in Pur\'e9
 so that she would easily be able to get information about Him. The Lord granted this last desire of His beloved mother. After this incidence the Lord started for Pur\'e9, leaving all the residents of Navadv\'e9
pa in an ocean of lamentation over His separation.
\par The Lord visited many important places on the way to Pur\'e9. He visited the temple of Gop\'e9n\'e4thaj\'e9, who had stolen condensed milk for His devotee \'c7r\'e9la M\'e4dhavendra Pur\'e9. Since then Deity Gop\'e9n\'e4thaj\'e9 is well known as K\'f1\'e9
ra-cor}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid7563248 a}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  Gop\'e9n\'e4
tha. The Lord relished this story with great pleasure. The propensity of stealing is there even in the absolute consciousness, but because this propensity is
 exhibited by the Absolute, it loses its perverted nature and thus becomes worshipable even by Lord Caitanya on the basis of the absolute consideration that the Lord and His stealing propensity are one and identical. This interesting story of Gop\'e9n\'e4
thaj\'e9 is vividly explained in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 by K\'e5\'f1\'ebad\'e4sa Kavir\'e4ja Gosv\'e4m\'e9.
\par After visiting the temple, of K\'f1\'e9ra-cor}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid7563248 a}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  Gop\'e9n\'e4tha of }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid7563248 Remuna}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
 at Balasore in Orissa, the Lord proceeded towards Pur\'e9 and on the way visited the temple of S\'e4k\'f1i Gop\'e4la, who appeared as a witness in the matter of two }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'eba }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 devotees' family quarrel. The Lord heard the story of S\'e4k\'f1i Gop\'e4la with great pleasure because He wanted to impress upon the atheists that the worshipable Deities in the temples approved by the great 
}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e4c\'e4ryas  }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 are not idols, as alleged by men with a poor fund of knowledge. The Deity in the temple is the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 arc\'e4}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
 incarnation of the Personality of Godhead, and thus the Deity is identical with the Lord in all respects. He responds to the proportion of the devotee's affection for Him. In the story of S\'e4k\'f1i Gop\'e4
la, in which there was a family misunderstanding by two devotees of the Lord, the Lord, in order to mitigate the turmoil as well as to show specific favor to His servitors, travelled from V\'e5nd\'e4vana to Vidy\'e4nagara, a 
village in Orissa, in the form of His }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 arc\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 incarnation. From there the Deity was brought to Cuttack, and thus the temple of S\'e4k\'f1i Gop\'e4
la is even today visited by thousands of pilgrims on the way to Jagann\'e4tha Pur\'e9. The Lord stayed overnight there and began to proceed toward Pur\'e9. On the way, His }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4sa }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 rod was broken by Nity\'e4nanda Prabhu. The Lord became apparently angry with him about this and went alone to Pur\'e9, leaving His companions behind.
\par At Pur\'e9, when He entered the temple of Jagann\'e4tha, He became 
