\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 "The conchshell and cowdung are bone and stool of two living beings. But because they have been recommended by the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 as pure, people accept them as such because of the authority of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas."
\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 The idea is that one cannot set his imperfect reason above the authority of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 The orders of the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
must be obeyed as they stand without any mundane reasoning. The so-called followers of the Vedic injunction make their own interpretations of the Vedic injunc
tions, and thus they establish different parties and sects of the Vedic religion. Lord Buddha directly denied the authority of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
and he established his own religion. Only for this reason the Buddhist religion was not accepted by the strict followers of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
But those who are so-called followers of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 are more harmful than the Buddhists. The Buddhists have the courage to deny the }{
