e parts and parcels are individual persons, the source of their emanation must not be impersonal. He is the Supreme Person amongst all the relative persons.
\par "The }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 inform us that from Him [}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723\charrsid7956946 Brahma}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1186441 n}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
] everything emanates, and on Him everything rests. And after annihilation, everything merges in Him only. Therefore, He is the ultimate dative, causative and accommodating cause of all causes. And all these causes cannot be attributed to an impersonal ob
ject.
\par "The }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
inform us that He alone became many, and when He so desires He glances over material nature. Before He glanced over material nature there was no material cosmic creation. Therefore, His glance is not material. Material mind or senses were u
nborn when the Lord glanced over material nature. Thus evidence in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
proves that beyond a doubt the Lord has transcendental eyes and a transcendental mind. They are not material. His impersonality therefore is a negation of His materiality, but not a denial of His transcendental personality.
\par "}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723\charrsid7956946 Brahma}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1186441 n}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  ultimately refers to the Personality of Godhead. Impersonal }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723\charrsid7956946 Brahma}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1186441 n}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  realization is just the negative conception of the mundane creations. Param\'e4tm\'e4 is the localized aspect of }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723\charrsid7956946 Brahma}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1186441 n}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  within all kinds of material bodies. Ultimately the Supreme }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723\charrsid7956946 Brahma}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1186441 n}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  realization is the realization of the Personality of Godhead according to all evidence of the revealed scriptures. He is the ultimate source of Vi\'f1\'ebu }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
tattvas.
\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 "The }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Pur\'e4\'ebas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 are also supplementary to the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas. }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 The Vedic }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 mantras }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 are too difficult for an ordinary man. Women, }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7\'fcdras }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and the so-called twice-born higher castes are unable to penetrate into the sense of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas. 
}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 And thus the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Itih\'e4sa }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Mah\'e4bh\'e4rata }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 as well as the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Pur\'e4\'ebas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 are made easy to explain the truths of the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 In his prayers before the boy \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Brahm\'e4 said that there is no limit to the fortune of the residents of Vrajabh\'fc
mi headed by \'c7r\'e9 Nanda Mah\'e4r\'e4ja and Ya\'e7od\'e4may\'e9 because the eternal Absolute Truth has become their intimate relative.
\par "The Vedic }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 mantra }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
maintains that the Absolute Truth has no legs and no hands and yet goes faster than all and accepts everything that is offered to Him in devotion. The latter statements definitely suggest the personal features of the Lord, although
 His hands and legs are distinguished from mundane hands and legs or other senses.
\par "}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723\charrsid7956946 Brahma}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1186441 n}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  is, therefore, never impersonal, but when such }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 mantras }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 are indirectly interpreted, it is wrongly thought that the Absolute Truth is impersonal. The Absolute Truth P
ersonality of Godhead is full of all opulences, and therefore He has a transcendental form of full existence, knowledge and bliss. How then can one establish that the Absolute Truth is impersonal?
\par "}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723\charrsid7956946 Brahma}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1186441 n}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 , being full of opulences, is understood to have ma
nifold energies, and all these energies are classified under three headings under the authority of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vi\'f1\'ebu Pur\'e4\'eba }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
(6.7.60), which says that the transcendental energies of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu are primarily three. His spiritual energy, as well as the energy of the livi
ng entities, are classified as superior energy, whereas the material energy is an inferior one which is sprouted out of ignorance.
\par "The energy of the living entities is technically called }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 k\'f1etraj\'efa }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 energy. This }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 k\'f1etraj\'efa-\'e7
akti, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 although equal in quality wi
th the Lord, becomes overpowered by material energy out of ignorance and thus suffers all sorts of material miseries. In other words, the living entities are located in the marginal energy between the superior spiritual and inferior material energy, and i
n proportion to the living being's contact with either the material or spiritual energies, the living entity is situated in proportionately higher and lower levels of existence.
\par "The Lord is beyond the inferior and marginal energies as above mentioned, and 
His spiritual energy is manifested in three different phases: as eternal existence, eternal bliss and eternal knowledge. As far as eternal existence is concerned, it is conducted by the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sandhin\'e9 }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 potency; similarly, bliss and knowledge are conducted by the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 hl\'e4dhin\'e9 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'e0vit }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
potencies respectively. As the supreme energetic Lord, He is the supreme controller of the spiritual, marginal and material energies. And all these different types of energies are connected with the Lord in eternal devotional service.
\par "
The Supreme Personality of Godhead is thus enjoying in His transcendental eternal form. Is it not astounding that one dares to call the Supreme Lord nonenergetic? The Lord is the controller of all energies, and the living entities are parts and parcels of
 one of the energies. Therefore there is a gulf of difference between the Lord and the living entities. How then can one say that the Lord and the living entities are one and the same? In the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g
\'e9t\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 also the living entities are described as bel
onging to the superior energy of the Lord. According to the principles of intimate correlation between the energy and the energetic, both of them are non-different also. Therefore, the Lord and the living entities are nondifferent as the energy and the en
ergetic.
\par "Earth, water, fire, air, ether, mind, intelligence and ego are all inferior energies of the Lord, but the living entities are different from all as superior energy. This is the version of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t
\'e4.
\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 "The transcendental form of the Lord is eter
nally existent and full of transcendental bliss. How then can such a form be a product of the material mode of goodness? Anyone, therefore, who does not believe in the form of the Lord is certainly a faithless demon and as such is untouchable, a not to be
 seen }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 persona non grata }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 fit to be punished by the Plutonic king.
\par "The Buddhists are called atheists because they have no respect for the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
but those who defy the Vedic conclusions, as above mentioned, under the pretense of being followers of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
are verily more dangerous than the Buddhists.
\par "\'c7r\'e9 Vy\'e4sadeva very kindly compiled the Vedic knowledge in his }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Ved\'e4nta-s\'fctra, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 but if one hears the commentation of the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9
 school (as represented by the \'c7a\'eckara }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 samprad\'e4ya) }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 certainly he will be misled on the path of spiritual realization.
\par "The theory of emanations is the beginning subject of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Ved\'e4nta-s\'fctra. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
All the cosmic manifestations are emanations from the Absolute Personality of Godhead by His inconceivable different energies. The example of the to
uchstone is applicable to the theory of emanation. The touchstone can convert an unlimited quantity of iron into gold, and still the touchstone remains as it is. Similarly, the Supreme Lord can produce all manifested worlds by His inconceivable energies, 
and yet He is full and unchanged. He is }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 p\'fcr\'eba }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 [complete], and although an unlimited number of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 p\'fcr
\'ebas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 emanate from Him, He is still }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 p\'fcr\'eba.
\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 "The theory of illusion of the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4da school is advocated on the ground that the theory of emanation will cause a transformation of the Absolute Truth. If that is the case, Vy\'e4
sadeva is wrong. To avoid this, they have skillfully brought in the theory of illusion. But the world or the cosmic creation is not false, as maintained by the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4da school. It simply has no per
manent existence. A nonpermanent thing cannot be called false altogether. But the conception that the material body is the self is certainly wrong.
\par }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid7956946 "Pra\'ebava [o}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 m] }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 omk\'e4ra }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is the primeval hymn. This transcendental sound is identical with t
he form of the Lord. All the Vedic hymns are based on this }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid7956946 p}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ra\'ebava omk\'e4ra. Tattvamasi }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
is but a side word in the Vedic literatures, and therefore this word cannot be the primeval hymn of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9p\'e4da }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid7956946\charrsid12326592 \'c7}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723\charrsid14297723 a\'eckar\'e4c\'e4rya}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  has given more stress on the side word }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 tattvamasi }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 than on the primeval principle }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 omk\'e4ra."
\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 The Lord thus spoke on the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Ved\'e4nta-s\'fctra }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and defied all the propaganda of the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4
da school.* }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10959717 
