\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 The Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4rya tried to defend himself and his M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4
da school by jugglery of logic and grammar, but the Lord was able to defeat him by His forceful arguments. He affirmed that we are all related with the Personality
 of Godhead eternally and that devotional service is our eternal function to exchange the dealings of our relations. And the result of such exchanges is to attain }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 prem\'e4 }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or love of Godhead. When love of Godhead is attained, love for all other beings automatically follows because the Lord is the sum total of all living beings.
\par The Lord said that but for these three items\emdash namely, eternal relation with God, exchange of dealings with Him and the attainment of love for Him\emdash all that is instructed in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is superfluous and concocted.
\par The Lord further added that the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4da philosophy taught by \'c7r\'e9p\'e4da }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10959717\charrsid12326592 \'c7}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723\charrsid14297723 a\'eckar\'e4c\'e4rya}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  is an imaginary explanation of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 but it had to be taught by him (}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10959717\charrsid12326592 \'c7}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723\charrsid14297723 a\'eckar\'e4c\'e4rya}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ) because he was ordered to teach it by the Personality of Godhead. In the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Padma Pur\'e4\'eba }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 it is stated that the Personality of Godhead ordered His Lordship \'c7
iva to deviate the human race from Him (the Personality of Godhead.) The Personality of Godhead was to be so covered so that people would be encouraged to generate more and more population. His Lordship \'c7iva said to Dev\'e9
: "In the Kali-yuga, I shall preach the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4da philosophy, which is nothing but clouded Buddhism, in the garb of a }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid6507282 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 "'
\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 After hearing all these speeches of the Lord \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu, the Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4
rya was struck with wonder and awe and regarded Him in dead silence. The Lord then encouraged him with assurance that there was no cause to wonder. "I say that }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 devotional service unt
o the Personality of Godhead is the highest goal of human life." }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 He then quoted a }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7loka }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 from the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bh\'e4gavatam }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
and assured him that even the liberated souls who are absorbed in the spirit and spiritual realization also take to the devotional service of the Lo
rd Hari because the Personality of Godhead has such transcendental qualities that He attracts the heart of the liberated soul too.
\par Then the Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4rya desired to listen to the explanation of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 "\'e4tm\'e4r\'e4ma" \'e7loka }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 from the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bh\'e4gavatam }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 (1.7.10). The Lord first of all asked Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4rya to explain it, and after that He would explain it. The Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4
rya then scholarly explained the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7loka }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 with special reference to logic. He explained the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7loka }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 in nine different ways chiefly based on logic because he was the most renowned scholar of logic of the time.
\par The Lord, after hearing the Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4rya, thanked him for the scholarly presentation of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7loka, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and then, at the request of the Bha\'f6\'f6
\'e4c\'e4rya, the Lord explained the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7loka }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 in sixty-four different ways without touching the nine explanations given by the Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4rya.

\par Thus after hearing the explanation of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e4tm\'e4r\'e4ma \'e7loka }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 from the Lord, the Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4
rya was convinced that such a scholarly presentation is impossible for an earthly creature.* }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid6507282 
