\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Before this \'c7r\'e9 Gop\'e9n\'e4tha \'c4c\'e4rya tried to convince him of the divinity of the Lord, but at that time he could not so accept Him. But the Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4
rya was astounded by the Lord's exposition of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Ved\'e4nta-s\'fctra }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and explanations of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e4tm\'e4r
\'e4ma \'e7loka, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and thus he began to think that he had committed a great offense at the lotus feet of the Lord by not recognizing Him to be K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a Himself. He then surrendered unto Him, repenting for his past dealings with Him, and the Lord was kind enough to accept the Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4rya. Out of His causeless mercy, the Lord manifested before him first as four-handed N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a and then again as two-handed Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba with a flute in His hand.
\par The Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4rya at once fell down at the lotus feet of the Lord and composed many suitable }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7lokas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
in praise of the Lord by His grace. He composed almost one hundred }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7lokas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
in praise of the Lord. The Lord then embraced him, and out of transcendental ecstasy the Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4rya lost consciousness of the physical state of life. Tears, trembling, throb
bing of the heart, perspiration, emotional waves, dancing, singing, crying and all the eight symptoms of trance were manifested in the body of the Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4rya. \'c7r\'e9 Gop\'e9n\'e4tha \'c4c\'e4
rya became very glad and astonished by this marvellous conversion of his brother-in-law by the grace of the Lord.
\par Out of the hundred celebrated }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7lokas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 composed by the Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4rya in praise of the Lord, the following two are most important, and these two }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7lokas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 explain the mission of the Lord in gist. They are as follows.
\par       1. Let me surrender unto the Personality of Godhead who has appeared now as Lord \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu. He is the ocean of all mercy and has come down to teach us material detachment, learning and devotional service to Himself.
\par       2. Since pure devotional service of the Lord has been lost in the oblivion of time, the Lord has appeared to renovate the principles, and therefore I offer my obeisances unto His lotus feet.
\par The Lord explained the word }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 mukti }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 to be equivalent to the word Vi\'f1\'ebu, or the Personality of Godhead. To attain }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 mukti }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or liberation from the bondage of material existence is to attain to the service of the Lord.
\par The Lord then proceeded towards South India for some time and converted everyone He met on the way to become devotees of Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Such devotees also converted many others to the cult of devotional service or to the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 of the Lord, and thus He reached the bank of the God\'e4var\'e9, where He met \'c7r\'e9la R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4
ya, the Governor of Madras on behalf of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Prat\'e4parudra, the King of Orissa. His talks with R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4
ya are very important for higher realization of transcendental knowledge, and the conversation itself forms a small booklet. We shall, however, give herewith a summary of the conversation.
\par \'c7r\'e9 R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4ya was a self-realized soul, although outwardly he belonged to a caste lower than the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'eba }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
in social status. He was not in the renounced order of life, and besides that he was a high government servant in the State. Still \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu accepted h
im as a liberated soul on the strength of the high order of his realization of transcendental knowledge. Similarly, the Lord accepted \'c7r\'e9la Harid\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4
kur, a veteran devotee of the Lord coming from a Mohammedan family. And there are many other great devot
ees of the Lord who came from different communities, sects and castes. The Lord's only criterion was the standard of devotional service of the particular person. He was not concerned with the outward dress of a man; He was concerned only with the inner so
ul and its activities. Therefore the whole missionary activities of the Lord are to be understood to be on the spiritual plane, and as such the cult of \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu or the cult of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bh
\'e4gavata-dharma }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 has nothing to do with mundane affairs, sociology, politics, economic development or any such sphere of life. }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is the purely transcendental urge of the soul.
\par When He met \'c7r\'e9 R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4ya on the bank of the God\'e4var\'e9, the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
followed by the Hindus was mentioned by the Lord. \'c7r\'e9la R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4ya said that by following the principles of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
the system of four castes and four orders of human life, everyone could realize transcendence. In the opinion of the Lord, the system of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is superficial onl
y, and it has very little to do with the highest realization of spiritual values. The highest perfection of life is to get detached from the material attachment and proportionately realize the transcendental loving service of the Lord. The Personality of 
Godhead recognizes a living being who is progressing in that line. Devotional service is, therefore, the culmination of the culture of all knowledge. When \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a the Supreme Personality of Godhead appeared for the deliverance of all fallen souls, He advi
sed the deliverance of all living entities as follows. The Supreme Absolute Personality of Godhead, from whom all living entities have emanated, must be worshiped by all their respective engagements, because everything that we see is also the expansion of
 His energy. That is the way of real perfection, and it is approved by all bona fide }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e4c\'e4ryas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 past and present. The system of }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is more or less based on moral and ethical principles. There is very little realization of the transcendence as such, and Lord \'c7r\'e9
 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu rejected it as superficial and asked R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4ya to go further into the matter.
\par \'c7r\'e9 R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4ya then suggested renunciation of fruitive actions unto the Lord. The }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
advises in this connection: "Whatever you d
o, whatever you eat and whatever you give, as well as whatever you perform in penance, offer to Me alone." This dedication on the part of the worker suggests that the Personality of Godhead is a step higher than the impersonal conception of the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
system, but still the relation of the living being and the Lord is not distinct in that way. The Lord therefore rejected this proposition and asked R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4ya to go further.
\par R\'e4ya then suggested renunciation of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and acceptance of de
votional service. The Lord did not approve of this suggestion also for the reason that all of a sudden one should not renounce his position, for that may not bring in the desired result.
\par It was further suggested by R\'e4ya that attainment of spiritual realiza
tion freed from the material conception of life is the topmost achievement for a living being. The Lord rejected this suggestion also because on the plea of such spiritual realization much havoc has been wrought by unscrupulous persons; therefore all of a
 sudden this is not possible. The R\'e4
ya then suggested sincere association of self-realized souls and hearing submissively the transcendental message of the pastimes of the Personality of Godhead. This suggestion was welcomed by the Lord. This suggestion was
 made following in the footsteps of Brahm\'e4j\'e9, who said that the Personality of Godhead is known as }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ajita }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
or the one who cannot be conquered or approached by anyone. But such }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ajita }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 also becomes }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 jita }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 (conquered) by one method, which is very simple and easy. 
The simple method is that one has to give up the arrogant attitude of declaring oneself to be God Himself. One must be very meek and submissive and try to live peacefully by lending the ear to the speeches of the transcendentally self-realized soul who sp
eaks on the message of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
or the religion of glorifying the Supreme Lord and His devotees. To glorify a great man is a natural instinct for living beings, but they have not learned to glorify the Lord. Perfection of life is attained simply by 
glorifying the Lord in association with a self-realized devotee of the Lord.* }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid11222877 
\par 
\par }{\f35\cf1\insrsid11222877\charrsid11222877 *The International Society for Krishna Consciousness is formed for this purpose.
