\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 The self-realized devotee is he who surrenders unto the Lord fully and who does not have attac
hment for material prosperity. Material prosperity and sense enjoyment and their advancement are all activities of ignorance in human society. Peace and friendship are impossible for a society detached from the association of God and His devotees. It is i
m
perative, therefore, that one should sincerely seek the association of pure devotees and hear them patiently and submissively from any position of life. The position of a person in the higher or lower status of life does not hamper one in the path of self
-realization. The only thing one has to do is to hear from a self-realized soul with a routine program. The teacher may also deliver lectures from the Vedic literatures, following in the footsteps of the bygone }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e4c\'e4ryas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 who realized the Absolute Truth. Lord \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu recommended this simple method of self-realization generally known as }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma. \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is the perfect guide for this purpose.
\par Above these topics discussed by the Lord and \'c7r\'e9 R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4ya, there were still more 
elevated spiritual talks between the two great personalities, and we purposely withhold those topics for the present because one has to come to the spiritual plane before further talks with R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4
ya can be heard. We have presented further talks of \'c7r\'e9la R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4ya with the Lord in another book }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 (Teachings of Lord Caitanya).
\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 At the conclusion of this meeting, \'c7r\'e9 R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4ya was advised by the Lord to retire from service and come to Pur\'e9 so that they could live together and relish a transcendenta
l relationship. Some time later, \'c7r\'e9 R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4ya retired from the Government service and took a pension from the King. He returned to his residence in Pur\'e9
, where he was one of the most confidential devotees of the Lord. There was another gentleman at Pur\'e9 of the name \'c7ikha M\'e4iti, who was also a confidante like R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4
ya. The Lord used to hold confidential talks on spiritual values with three or four companions at Pur\'e9, and He passed eighteen years in that way in spiritual trance. His talks were recorded by His private secretary \'c7r\'e9 D\'e4modara Gosv\'e4m\'e9
, one of the four most intimate devotees.
\par The Lord extensively travelled all over the southern part of India. The great saint of Mah\'e4r\'e4\'f1\'f6ra, known as saint Tuk\'e4r\'e4m, was also initiated by the Lord. Saint Tuk\'e4r\'e4
m, after initiation by the Lord, overflooded the whole of the Mah\'e4r\'e4\'f1\'f6ra Province with the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
movement, and the transcendental flow is still rolling on in the southwestern part of the great Indian peninsula.
\par The Lord excavated from South India two very important old literatures, namely the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4 * }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 K\'e5\'f1\'eba-kar\'eb\'e4m\'e5ta, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and these two valuable }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid9851517 
\par 
\par }{\f35\cf1\insrsid9851517\charrsid9851517 *Summary of }{\i\f35\cf1\insrsid9851517\charrsid9851517 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam.}{\f35\cf1\insrsid9851517\charrsid9851517 
