\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 books are authorized studies for the person in the devotional line. The Lord then returned to Pur\'e9 after His South Indian tour.
\par On His return to Pur\'e9, all the anxious devotees of the Lord got back their life, and the Lord remained there with continued pastimes of His transcendental realizations. The most important incidence during that time was His gra
nting audience to King Prat\'e4parudra. King Prat\'e4parudra was a great devotee of the Lord, and he considered himself to be one of the servants of the Lord entrusted with sweeping}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid11222877  the temple. This submissive at}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 titude of the King was very much appreciated by \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu. The King requested both Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4rya and R\'e4
ya to arrange his meeting with the Lord. When, however, the Lord was petitioned by His two stalwart devotees, He flatly refused to grant the request, even though it was put forward by personal associates like R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4ya and S\'e4rvabhauma Bha
\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4rya. The Lord maintained that it is dangerous for a }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
to be in intimate touch with worldly money conscious men and with women. The Lord was an ideal }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 No woman could approach the Lord 
even to offer respects. Women's seats were accommodated far away from the Lord. As an ideal teacher and }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e4c\'e4rya, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
He was very strict in the routine work of a }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Apart from being a divine incarnation, the Lord was an ideal character as a human being. H
is behavior with other persons was also above suspicion. In His dealing as }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e4c\'e4rya, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
He was harder than the thunderbolt and softer than the rose. One of His associates, Junior Harid\'e4sa, committed a great mistake by lustfully glancing at a young woman, and the Lord as Supersoul could detect this just in the mind of Junior Harid\'e4
sa. He was at once banished from His association and was never accepted again, even though He was implored to excuse Harid\'e4sa for the mistake. Junior Harid\'e4sa afterwards committed suici
de due to being disassociated from the company of the Lord, and the news of suicide was duly related to the Lord. Even at that time the Lord was not forgetful of the offense, and He said that Harid\'e4sa had rightly met with the proper punishment.
\par On the prin
ciples of the renounced order of life and discipline, the Lord knew no compromise, and therefore even though He knew that the King was a great devotee, He refused to see the King only because the King was a dollar and cent man. By this example the Lord wa
n
ted to emphasize the proper behavior for a transcendentalist. A transcendentalist has nothing to do with women and money. He must always refrain from such intimate relations. The King was, however, favored by the Lord by the expert arrangement of the devo
t
ees. This means that the beloved devotee of the Lord can favor a neophyte more liberally than the Lord. Pure devotees, therefore, never commit an offense at the feet of another pure devotee. An offense at the lotus feet of the Lord is sometimes excused by
 the merciful Lord, but an offense at the feet of a devotee is very dangerous for one who actually wants to make progress in devotional service.
\par As long as the Lord remained at Pur\'e9, thousands of His devotees used to come to see Him during the Ratha-y\'e4tr\'e4 car festival of Lord Jagann\'e4tha. And during the car festival, the washing of the Gu\'eb\'f2ic\'e4
 temple under the direct supervision of the Lord was an important function. The Lord's congregational }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 movement at Pur\'e9
 was a unique exhibition for the mass of people. That is the way to turn the mass mind towards spiritual realization. The Lord inaugurated this system of mass }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and leaders of all countries can take advantage of this spiritual movement in order to keep the mass of people in a pure stat
e of peace and friendship with one another. This is now the demand of the present human society all over the world.
\par After some time the Lord again started on his tour towards Northern India, and He decided to visit V\'e5nd\'e4vana and its neighboring places. He passed through the jungles of Jharikha\'eb\'f2a (Madhya Bh\'e4rat), and all the wild animals also joined His 
}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 movement. The wild tigers, elephants, bears and deer all together accompanied the Lord, and the Lord accompanied them in }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 By this He proved that by the propagation of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 movement (congregational chanting and glorifying the name of the Lord) even the wild animals can live in peace and friendship, and what to speak of men who are supposed to be civilized. No man in the world wi
ll refuse to join the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 movement. Nor is the Lord's }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 movement restricted to any caste, creed, color or species. Here is direct evidence of His great mission: He allowed even the wild animals to partake in His great movement.
\par On His way back from V\'e5nd\'e4vana He first came to Pray\'e4g, where He met R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9 along with his younger brother Anupama. Then He came down to Benares. For two months, He instructed \'c7r\'e9 San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 in the transcendental science. The instruction to San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9 is in itself a long narration, and full presentation of the instruction will not be possible here. The main ideas are given as follows.
\par San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9 (formerly known as Dabir Kh\'e4s) was in the cabinet service of the Bengal Government under the regime of Nawab Husain Shah. He decided to join with the Lord and thus retired from the service. On His way back from V\'e5nd\'e4
vana, when He reached V\'e4r\'e4\'ebas\'e9, the Lord became the guest of \'c7r\'e9 Tapana Mi\'e7ra and Candra\'e7ekhara, assisted by a Mah\'e4r\'e4\'f1\'f6ra }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'eba. }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 At that time V\'e4r\'e4\'ebas\'e9 was headed by a great }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 of the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4da school named 
\'c7r\'e9p\'e4da Prak\'e4\'e7\'e4nanda Sarasvat}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid9851517\charrsid12326592 \'e9}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 . When the Lord was at V\'e4r\'e4\'ebas\'e9
, the people in general became more attracted to Lord Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu on account of His mass }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 movement. Wher
ever He visited, especially the Vi\'e7van\'e4tha temple, thousands of pilgrims would follow Him. Some were attracted by His bodily features, and others were attracted by His melodious songs glorifying the Lord.
\par The M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9s }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 designate themselves as N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. V\'e4r\'e4\'ebas\'e9 is still overflooded with many M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 
}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9s. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Some people who saw the Lord in His }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 party considered Him to be actually N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, and this report reached the camp of the great }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9 }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Prak\'e4\'e7\'e4nanda.
\par In India there is always a kind of spiritual rivalry between the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4da and }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bh\'e4gavata}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  schools, and thus when the news of the Lord reached Prak
\'e4\'e7\'e4nanda he knew that the Lord was a Vai\'f1\'ebava }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and therefore he minimized the value of the Lord before 
