\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 "So on th
e order of my spiritual master, I chant the holy name of Hari, and I am now mad after this holy name. Whenever I utter the holy name I forget Myself completely, and sometimes I laugh, cry and dance like a madman. I thought that I had actually gone mad by 
t
his process of chanting, and therefore I asked My spiritual master about it. He informed Me that this was the real effect of chanting the holy name, which produces a transcendental emotion that is a rare manifestation. It is the sign of love of God, which
 is the ultimate end of life. Love of God is transcendental to liberation }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 [mukti], }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and thus it is called the fifth stage of}{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 spiritual realization, above the stage of liberation. By chanting the holy name of K\'e5\'f1\'eba one attains the stage of love of God, and it
 was good that fortunately I was favored with the blessing."
\par On hearing this statement from the Lord, the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 asked the Lord what was the harm in studying the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Ved\'e4nta }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 along with chanting the holy name. Prak\'e4\'e7\'e4nanda Sarasvat\'e9 knew well that the Lord was formerly known as Nim\'e4i Pa\'eb\'f2
it, a very learned scholar of Navadv\'e9pa, and His posing as a great fool was certainly to some purpose. Hearing this inquiry by the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
the Lord smiled and said, "My dear sir, if you do not mind, I will answer your inquiry."
\par All the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9s }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
there were very much pleased with the Lord for His honest dealings, and they unanimously replied that they would not be offended by whatever He replied. The Lord then spoke as follows:
\par }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 "Ved\'e4nta-s\'fctra }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is comprised of transcendental words or sounds uttered by the transcendental Personality of Godhead. As such, in the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Ved\'e4nta }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 there cannot be any human deficiencies like mistake, illusion cheating or inefficiency. The message of the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Upani\'f1ads }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is expressed in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Ved\'e4nta-s\'fctra, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and 
what is said there directly is certainly glorified. Whatever interpretations have been given by }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid5114256\charrsid12326592 \'c7}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723\charrsid14297723 a\'eckar\'e4c\'e4rya}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  have no direct bearing on the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 s\'fctra, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and therefore such commentation spoils everything.
\par "The word }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723\charrsid5114256 Brahma}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid5114256 n}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  indicates the greatest of all, which is full with transcendental opulences, superior to all. }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723\charrsid5114256 Brahma}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid5114256 n}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
 is ultimately the Personality of Godhead, and He is covered by indirect interpretations and established as impersonal. Everything that is in the spiritual
 world is full of transcendental bliss, including the form, body, place and paraphernalia of the Lord. All are eternally cognizant and blissful. It is not the fault of the \'c4c\'e4rya \'c7a\'eckara that he has so interpreted }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Ved\'e4nta, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 but if someone accepts it, then c
ertainly he is doomed. Anyone who accepts the transcendental body of the Personality of Godhead as something mundane certainly commits the greatest blasphemy."
\par The Lord thus spoke to the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 almost in the same way that He spoke to the Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4rya of Pur\'e9
, and by forceful arguments He nullified the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4da interpretations of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Ved\'e4nta-s\'fctra. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 All the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9s }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 there claimed that the Lord was the personified }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and the Personality of Godhead. All the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9s }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 were converted to the cult of }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 bhakti, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and all of them accepted the holy name of the Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, and they dined together with the Lord in the midst of them. After this conversion of the}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  sanny\'e4s\'e9s, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 the popularity of the Lord increased at V\'e4r
\'e4\'ebas\'e9, and thousands of people assembled to see the Lord in person. The Lord thus established the primary importance of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavata-dharma, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and He defeated all other systems of spiritual realization. Since then everyone at V\'e4r\'e4\'ebas\'e9 was overwhelmed with the transcendental }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9
rtana }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 movement.
\par While the Lord was camping at V\'e4r\'e4\'ebas\'e9, San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 also arrived after retiring from office. He was formerly one of the state ministers in the government of Bengal, then under the regime of Nawab Hussain Shah. He had some difficulty in getting relief from the s
tate service, for the Nawab was reluctant to let him leave. Nonetheless he came to V\'e4r\'e4\'ebas\'e9
, and the Lord taught him the principles of devotional service. He taught him about the constitutional position of the living being, the cause of his bondage under m
aterial conditions, his eternal relation with the Personality of Godhead, the transcendental position of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, His expansions in different plenary portions of incarnations, His control of different parts of the universe, the 
n
ature of His transcendental abode, devotional activities, their different stages of development and the rules and regulations for achieving the gradual stages of spiritual perfection, the symptoms of different incarnations in different ages and how to det
ect them with reference to the context of revealed scriptures.
\par The Lord's teachings to San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9 form a big chapter in the text of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
and to explain the whole teachings in minute details will require a volume in itself. These are treated in detail in our book }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Teachings of Lord Caitanya.
\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 At Mathur\'e4, the Lord visited all the important places; then He reached V\'e5nd\'e4vana. Lord Caitanya appeared in the family of a high caste }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'eb
a, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and over and above that as }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sanny\'e4s\'e9 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 He was the preceptor for all the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 var\'ebas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e4\'e7ramas. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
But He used to accept meals from all classes of Vai\'f1\'ebavas. At Mathur\'e4 the Sanodhia }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'ebas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
are considered to be in the lower status of society, but the Lord accepted meals in their families also because His host happened to be a disciple of the M\'e4dhavendra Pur\'e9 family.
\par At V\'e5nd\'e4vana the Lord took bath in twenty-four important bathing places and ghats. He travelled to all the twelve important }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 vanas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
(forests). In these forests all the cows and birds welcomed Him, as if H
e were their very old friend. The Lord also began to embrace all the trees of those forests, and by doing so He felt the symptoms of transcendetnal ecstasy. Sometimes He fell unconscious, but He was made to regain consciousness by the chanting of the holy
 name of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. The transcendental symptoms that were visible on the body of the Lord during His travel within the forest of V\'e5nd\'e4vana were all unique and inexplicable, and we have just given a synopsis only.
\par Some of the important places that were visited by the Lord in V\'e5nd\'e4vana were K}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid5114256 a}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 myavana, \'c4d\'e9\'e7vara, Pabansarovara, Khadirvana, \'c7e\'f1a\'e7\'e4y\'e9, Khelat\'e9
rtha, Bhandirvana, Bhadravana, \'c7r\'e9vana. Lauhavana, Mah\'e4vana, Gokula, Kaliyahrada, Dv\'e4da\'e7\'e4ditya, Ke\'e7\'e9t\'e9rtha, etc. When He saw the place where the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 r\'e4sa }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 dance took place, He at once fell down in trance. As long as He remained at V\'e5nd\'e4vana, He made His headquarters at Akr}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid5114256 u}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
r Ghat.
\par From V\'e5nd\'e4vana His personal servitor K\'e5\'f1\'ebad\'e4sa Vipra induced Him to go back to Pray\'e4g to take bath during the M\'e4gha Mel\'e4. The Lord acceded to this proposal, and they started for Pray\'e4
g. On the way they were met with some Pathans, amongst whom there was a learned Moulana. The Lord had some talks with the Moulana and his companions, and the Lord convinced the Moulana that in the Koran also there are descriptions of }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and K\'e5\'f1\'eba. All the Pathans were converted to His cult of devotional service.
\par When He returned to Pray\'e4g, \'c7r\'e9la R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9 and his youngest brother met Him near Bindu-m\'e4dhava Temple. This time the Lord was welcomed by the people of Pray\'e4g more respectfully. Vallabha Bha\'f6\'f6
a, who resided on the other bank of Pray\'e4g in the village of Arail, was to receive Him at his place, but while going there the Lord jumped in the River Yamun\'e4. With great difficulty He was picked up in 
an unconscious state. Finally He visited the headquarters of Vallabha Bha\'f6\'f6a. This Vallabha Bha\'f6\'f6a was one of His chief admirers, but later on he inaugurated his own party of the Vallabha }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
samprad\'e4ya.
\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 On the bank of the Da\'e7\'e4\'e7vamedha Ghat at Pray\'e4g for ten days continually the Lord instructed R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9 in the science of devotional service of the Lord. He taught the Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 the divisions of the living creatures in the 8,400,000 species of life. Then He taught him about the human species. Out of them He disc
ussed the followers of the Vedic principles, out of them the fruitive workers, out of them the empiric philosophers, and out of them the liberated souls. He said that there are only a few who are actually pure devotees of Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba.

\par \'c7r\'e9la R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9 was the younger brother of San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9
, and when he retired from service he brought with him two boatfuls of gold coins. This means that he brought with him some hundreds of thousands of rupees accumulated by the labor of his service. And before leaving home for Lord Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu, he divided the wealth as follows: fifty percent for the service of the Lord and His devotees, twenty-five percent for relatives and twenty-five percent for his personal needs in case of emergency . In that way he set 
an example for all householders.
\par The Lord taught the Gosv\'e4m\'e9 about devotional service, comparing it to a creeper, and He advised him to protect the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 bhakti }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
creeper most carefully against the mad elephant offense against the pure devotees. In addition, the creeper has to be protected from the desires of sense enjoyment, monistic liberation and perfection of the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 hatha-yoga }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 system. They are all detrimental on the path of devotional service. Similarly, violence against living beings, desire for worldly gain, wor
ldly reception and worldly fame are all detrimental to the progress of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 bhakti }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma.

\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Pure devotional service must be freed from all desires for se
nse gratification, fruitive aspirations and culture of monistic knowledge. One must be freed from all kinds of designations, and when one is thus converted into transcendental purity, one can then serve the Lord by purified senses.
\par As long as there is the desire to enjoy sensually or to become one with the Supreme or to possess the mystic powers, there is no question of attaining the stage of pure devotional service.
\par Devotional service is conducted under two categories, namely primary practice and spontaneo
us emotion. When one can rise up to the platform of spontaneous emotion, he can make further progress by spiritual attachment, feeling, love, and many higher stages of devotional life for which there are no English words. We have tried to explain the scie
nce of devotional service in our book }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 The Nectar of Devotion }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 based on the authority of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhakti-ras\'e4m\'e5
ta-sindhu }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 by \'c7r\'e9la R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9.
\par }\pard \qj \li284\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin284\itap0\pararsid12326592 {\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Transcendental devotional service has five stages of reciprocation.
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12326592 {\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 1. The self-realization stage just after liberation from the material bondage is called the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7\'e4nta }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or neutral stage.
\par 2. After that, when there is development of transcendental knowledge of the Lord's internal opulences, the devotee engages himself in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 d\'e4sya }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 stage.

\par 3. By further development of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 d\'e4sya }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 stage,
 a respectful fraternity with the Lord develops, and above that a feeling of friendship on equal terms becomes manifest. Both these stages are called }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 s\'e4khya }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 stage, or devotional service in friendship.
\par 4. Above this there is the stage of paternal affection toward the Lord and this is called the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 v\'e4tsalya }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 stage.
\par 5. And above this stage there is the stage of conjugal love, and this stage is called the highest stage of love of God, although there is no difference in quality in any of the above stages. The last stage of conjugal love of God is called the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 m\'e4dhurya }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 stage.
\par Thus He instructed R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9 in devotional science and deputed him to V\'e5nd\'e4vana to excavate the lost sites of the transcendental pastimes of the Lord. After this, the Lord returned to V\'e4r\'e4\'ebas\'e9 and delivered the}{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  sanny\'e4s\'e9s }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and instructed the elder brother of R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9. We have already discussed this.
\par The Lord left only eight }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7lokas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 of His instructions in writing, and they are known as the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7ik\'f1\'e4
\'f1\'f6akam. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 All other literatures of His divine cult were extensively written by the Lord's principal followers, the six Gosv\'e4m\'e9s of V\'e5nd\'e4
vana, and their followers. The cult of Caitanya philosophy is richer than any other, and it is admitted to be the living religion of the day with the potency for spreading as }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vi\'e7va-dharma }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or universal religion. We are glad that the matter has been taken up by some enthusiastic sages like Bhaktisiddh\'e4nta Sarasvat\'e9 Gosv\'e4m\'e9 Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja and his disciples. We shall eagerly wait for the happy days of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 prema-dharma }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 inaugurated by the Lord \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu.
\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4026791 
\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 The eight }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7lokas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 completed by the Lord are:
\par }\pard \qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4026791 {\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 1.
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12326592 {\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Glory to the \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9rtana, }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 which cleanses the heart of all the dust accumulated for years and extinguishes the fire of conditional life, of repeated birth and death. This }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sa\'eck\'e9
rtana }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 movement is the prime benediction for humanity at large because it spreads the rays of the benedictio
n moon. It is the life of all transcendental knowledge. It increases the ocean of transcendental bliss, and it enables us to fully taste the nectar for which we are always anxious.
\par }\pard \qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4026791 {\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 2.
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12326592 {\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 O my Lord, Your holy name alone can render all benediction to living beings, and thus You have hundreds and millions of names like K
\'e5\'f1\'eba and Govinda. In these transcendental names You have invested all Your transcendental energies. There are not even hard and fast rules for chanting these names. O my Lord, out of kindness You enable us to easily approach You }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 by}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  chanting Your holy names, but I am so unfortunate that I have no attraction for them.
\par }\pard \qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4026791 {\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 3.
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12326592 {\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 One should chant the holy name of the Lord in a humble state of mind, thinking oneself lower than the straw in the street; one shou
ld be more tolerant than a tree, devoid of all sense of false prestige and should be ready to offer all respect to others. In such a state of mind one can chant the holy name of the Lord constantly.
\par }\pard \qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4026791 {\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 4.
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12326592 {\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 O almighty Lord, I have no desire to accumulate wealth
, nor do I desire beautiful women, nor do I want any number of followers. I only want Your causeless devotional service birth after birth.
\par }\pard \qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4026791 {\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 5.
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12326592 {\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 O son of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Nanda [K\'e5\'f1\'eba], I am Your eternal servitor, yet somehow or other I have fallen into the ocean of 
birth and death. Please pick me up from this ocean of death and place me as one of the atoms of Your lotus feet.
\par }\pard \qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4026791 {\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 6.
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12326592 {\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
