\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12326592 {\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Obeisances unto the Personality of Godhead, V\'e4sudeva, directly indicate Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, who is the divine son of Vasudeva and Devak\'e9. This fact will be more explicitly explained in the text of this work. \'c7r\'e9 Vy\'e4sadeva asserts herein that \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the original Per
sonality of Godhead, and all others are His direct or indirect plenary portions or portions of the portion. \'c7r\'e9la J\'e9va Gosv\'e4m\'e9 has even more explicitly explained the subject matter in his }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 K
\'e5\'f1\'eba-sandarbha. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 And Brahm\'e4, the original living being, has explained the subject of \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba substantially in his treatise named }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 In the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 S\'e4ma-veda Upani\'f1ad, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 it is also stated that Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a is the divine son of Devak\'e9. Therefore, in this prayer, the first proposition holds that Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the p
rimeval Lord, and if any transcendental nomenclature is to be understood as belonging to the Absolute Personality of Godhead, it must be the name indicated by the word K\'e5\'f1\'eba, which means the all-attractive. In }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 in many places, the Lord assert
s Himself to be the original Personality of Godhead, and this is confirmed by Arjuna, and also by great sages like N\'e4rada, Vy\'e4sa, and many others. In the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Padma Pur\'e4\'eba, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 it is also stated that out of the innumerable names of the Lord, the name of K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the principal one. V\'e4
sudeva indicates the plenary portion of the Personality of Godhead, and all the different forms of the Lord, being identical with V\'e4sudeva, are indicated in this text. The name V\'e4sudeva particularly indicates the divine son of Vasudeva and Devak\'e9
. \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba is always meditated upon by the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 paramaha\'e0sas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 who are the perfected ones among those in the renounced order of life.
\par V\'e4sudeva, or Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba, is the cause of all causes. Everything that exists emanates from the Lord. How this is so is explained in later chapters of this work. This work is described by Mah\'e4prabhu \'c7r\'e9
 Caitanya as the spotless }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Pur\'e4\'eba }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 because it contains the transcendental narration of the Personality of Godhead \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. The history of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is also very glorious. It was compiled by \'c7r\'e9 Vy\'e4
sadeva after he had attained maturity in transcendental knowledge. He wrote this under the instructions of \'c7r\'e9 N\'e4radaj\'e9, his spiritual master. Vy\'e4sadeva compiled all Vedic literatures containing the four divisions of the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Ved\'e4nta-s\'fctras }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Brahma-s\'fctras, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Pur\'e4\'ebas, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Mah\'e4bh\'e4rata, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and so on. But nevertheless he was not satisfied. His dissatisfaction was observed by his spiritual master, and thus N\'e4
rada advised him to write on the transcendental activities of Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. These transcendental activities are described specifically in the Tenth Canto of this work. But, in order to reach to the very substance, one must proceed gradually by developing knowledge of the categories.
\par It is natural that a philo
sophical mind wants to know about the origin of the creation. At night he sees the stars in the sky, and he naturally speculates about their inhabitants. Such inquiries are natural for man because man has a developed consciousness which is higher than tha
t of the animals. The author of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 gives a direct answer to such inquiries. He says that the Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a is the origin of all creations. He is not only the creator of the universe, but the destroyer as well. The manifested cosmic nature is
 created at a certain period by the will of the Lord. It is maintained for some time, and then it is annihilated by His will. Therefore, the supreme will is behind all cosmic activities. Of course, there are atheists of various catagories who do not belie
v
e in a creator, but that is due to a poor fund of knowledge. The modern scientist, for example, has created space satellites, and by some arrangement or other, these satellites are thrown into outer space to fly for some time at the control of the scienti
st who is far away. Similarly, all the universes with innumerable stars and planets are controlled by the intelligence of the Personality of Godhead.
\par In Vedic literatures, it is said that the Absolute Truth, Personality of Godhead, is the chief amongst all living personalities. All living beings beginning from the first created being, Brahm\'e4
, down to the smallest ant are individual living beings. And above Brahm\'e4, there are even other living beings with individual capacities, and the Personality of Godhead i
s also a similar living being. And He is an individual as are the other living beings. But the Supreme Lord or the supreme living being has the greatest intelligence, and He possesses supermost inconceivable energies of all different varieties. If a man's
 
brain can produce a space satellite, one can very easily imagine how brains higher than man can produce similarly wonderful things which are far superior. The reasonable person will easily accept this argument, but there are stubborn atheists who would ne
ver agree. \'c7r\'e9la Vy\'e4sadeva, however, at once accepts the supreme intelligence as the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 parame\'e7vara. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
He offers his respectful obeisances unto the supreme intelligence addressed as the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 para }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 parame\'e7
vara }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or the Supreme Personality of Godhead. And that }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 parame\'e7vara }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, as admitted in }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and other scriptures delivered by \'c7r\'e9 Vy\'e4sadeva and specifically in this }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 In }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
the Lord says that there is no other }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Para-tattva (summum bonum) }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 than Himself. Therefore, \'c7r\'e9 Vy\'e4sadeva at once worships the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Para-tattva, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba, whose transcendental activities are described in the Tenth Canto.
\par Unscrupulous persons go immediately to the Tenth Canto and especially to the five chapters which describe the Lord's }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 r\'e4sa dance. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 This portion of the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
the most confidential part of this great literature. Unless one is thoroughly accomplished in the transcendental knowledge of the Lord, one is sure to misunderstand the Lord's worshipable transcendental pastimes called }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 r\'e4sa }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 dance and His love affairs with the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 gop\'e9s. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
This subject matter is highly spiritual, and only the liberated persons who have gradually attained to the stage of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 paramaha\'e0sa }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
can transcendentally relish this }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 r\'e4sa }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 dance. \'c7r\'e9la Vy\'e4sadeva therefore gives the rea
der the chance to gradually develop spiritual realization before actually relishing the essence of the pastimes of the Lord. Therefore, he purposely invokes a }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 G\'e4yatr\'e9 mantra, dh\'e9mahi. }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 This }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 G\'e4yatr\'e9 mantra }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is meant for spiritually advanced people. When one is successful in chanting the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 G\'e4yatr\'e9 mantra, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
he can enter into the transcendental position of the Lord. One must therefore acquire brahminical qualities or be perfectly situated in the quality of goodness in order to chant the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 G\'e4yatr\'e9 mantra }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 successfully and then attain to the stage of transcendentally realizing the Lord, His name, His fame, His qualities and so on.
\par }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is the narration of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 svar\'fcpa }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 of the Lord manifested by His internal potency, and this potency is distinguished from the external potency which has manifested the cosmic world, which is within our experience. \'c7r\'e9la Vy\'e4
sadeva makes a clear distinction between the two in this }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7loka. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9 Vy\'e4
sadeva says herein that the manifested internal potency is real, whereas the external mani
fested energy in the form of material existence is only temporary and illusory like the mirage in the desert. In the desert mirage there is no actual water. There is only the appearance of water. Real water is somewhere else. The manifested cosmic creatio
n
 appears as reality. But reality, of which this is but a shadow, is in the spiritual world. Absolute Truth is in the spiritual sky, not the material sky. In the material sky everything is relative truth. That is to say, one truth depends on something else
.
 This cosmic creation results from interaction of the three modes of nature, and the temporary manifestations are so created as to present an illusion of reality to the bewildered mind of the conditioned soul, who appears in so many species of life, inclu
ding the higher demigods, like Brahm\'e4
, Indra, Candra, and so on. In actuality, there is no reality in the manifested world. There appears to be reality, however, because of the true reality which exists in the spiritual world, where the Personality of Godhe
ad eternally exists with His transcendental paraphernalia.
\par The chief engineer of a complicated construction does not personally take part in the construction, but he knows every nook and corner because everything is done under his direction. He knows every
thing about the construction, both directly and indirectly. Similarly, the Personality of Godhead who is the supreme engineer of this cosmic creation knows every nook and corner, although affairs are being carried out by demigods. Beginning from Brahm\'e4
 dow
n to the insignificant ant, no one is independent in the material creation. The hand of the Lord is seen everywhere. All material elements as well as all spiritual sparks emanate from Him only. And whatever is created in this material world is but the int
eraction of two energies, the material and the spiritual, which emanate from the Absolute Truth, the Personality of Godhead, \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. A chemist can manufacture water in the chemical laboratory by mixing hydrogen and oxygen. But, in reality, the living ent
ity works in the laboratory under the direction of the Supreme Lord. And the materials with which he works are also supplied by the Lord. The Lord knows everything directly and indirectly, and He is cognizant of all minute details, and He is fully indepen
d
ent. He is compared with the mine of gold, and the cosmic creations in so many different forms are compared with objects made from the gold, such as gold rings, necklaces and so on. The gold ring and the gold necklace are qualitatively one with the gold i
n the mine, but quantitatively the gold in the mine is different. Therefore, the Absolute Truth is simultaneously one and different. Nothing is absolutely equal with the Absolute Truth, but at the same time, nothing is independent of the Absolute Truth.

\par Conditioned souls beginning from Brahm\'e4
, who engineers the entire universe, down to the insignificant ant, are all creating, but none of them are independent of the Supreme Lord. The materialist wrongly thinks that there is no creator other than his own self. This is called }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 m\'e4y\'e4, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or illusion.
\par Because of his poor fund of knowledge, the materialist cannot see beyond the purview of his imperfect senses, and thus he thinks that matter automatically takes its own shape without the aid of a superior intelligence. This is refuted in this }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7loka }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 by \'c7r\'e9la Vy\'e4
sadeva: "Since the complete whole or the Absolute Truth is the source of everything, nothing can be independent of the body of the Absolute Truth." Whatever happens to the body quickly becomes known to the embodied. 
Similarly, the creation is the body of the absolute whole. Therefore, the Absolute knows everything directly and indirectly that happens in the creation.
\par In the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7ruti mantra, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 it is also stated that the absolute whole or }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723\charrsid739375 Brahma}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1186441 n}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  is the ultimate source of everything. Everything emanates from Him, and everything is maintained by Him. And at the end, everything enters into Him. That is the law of nature. In the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Sm\'e5ti mantra, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 the same is confirmed. It is said that the source from which everything emanates at the beginning of Brahm\'e4
's millennium, and the reservoir to which everything ultimately enters, is the Absolute Truth or }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid14297723\charrsid739375 Brahma}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1186441 n}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
. Material scientists take it for granted that the ultimate source of the planetary system is the sun, but they are unable to explain the source of the sun. Herein, the ultimate source is explained. According to the Vedic literatures, Brahm\'e4
, who may be compared to the sun, is not the ultimate creator. It is stated in this }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7loka }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 that Brahm\'e4 was taught Vedic knowledge by the Personality
 of Godhead. One may argue that Brahm\'e4, being the original living being, could not be inspired because there was no other being living at that time. Herein it is stated that the Supreme Lord inspired the secondary creator, Brahm\'e4
, in order that Brahm\'e4 could carry out his creative functions. So, the supreme intelligence behind all creations is the Absolute Godhead, \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba. In }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba states that it is He only who superintends the creative energy, }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 prak\'e5ti, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
which constitutes the totality of matter. Therefore, \'c7r\'e9 Vy\'e4sadeva does not worship Brahm\'e4, but the Supreme Lord, who guides Brahm\'e4 in his creative activities. In this }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7loka, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 the particular words }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 abhij}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid8727686\charrsid12326592 \'efa\'f9}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 svar\'e4\'f6 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 are significant. T
hese two words distinguish the Supreme Lord from all the other living entities. No other living entity is either }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 abhij\'efa\'f9 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 svar\'e4\'f6. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Namely, no one is either fully cognizant or fully independent. Even Brahm\'e4 has to meditate upon the Supreme Lord in order t
o create. Then what to speak of great scientists like Einstein! The brains of such a scientist are certainly not the products of any human being. Scientists cannot manufacture such a brain, and what to speak of foolish atheists who defy the authority of t
he Lord? Even M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 impersonalists who flatter themselves that they can become one with the Lord are neither }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 abhij\'efa\'f9 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 nor }{
