d into four castes and four orders of life. The four castes are the intelligent caste, the martial caste, the productive caste and the laborer caste. These castes are classified in terms of one's work and qualification, and not by birth. Then again there 
a
re four orders of life, namely the student life, the householder's life, the retired and the devotional life. In the best interest of human society there must be such divisions of life, otherwise no social institution can grow up in a healthy state. And i
n each and every one of the above-mentioned divisions of life, }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 the aim must be to please the supreme authority of the Personality of Godhead. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
This institutional function of human society is known as the system of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 which is quite natural for the civilized life. The }{
