institution is constructed to enable one to realize the Absolute Truth. It is not for artificial domination of one division over the other. When the aim of life, i.e., realization of the Absolute Truth, is missed by too much attachment for }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 indriya-pr\'e9ti }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or sense gratification, as it is already discussed hereinbefore, the institution of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 var
\'eb\'e4\'e7rama }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is utilized by selfish men to pose an artificial predominance over the weaker section. In the Kali-yuga, or in the age of 
quarrel, this artificial predominance is already current, but the saner section of the people know it well that the division of castes and orders of life are meant for smooth social intercourse and high thinking self-realization and not for any other purp
ose.
\par Herein the statement of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bh\'e4gavatam }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is that the highest aim of life or the highest perfection of the institution of the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is to cooperate jointly for the satisfaction of the Supreme Lord, which is also confirmed in the }{
