represented by the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7\'e4lagr\'e4ma-\'e7il\'e4, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and so also some of the higher castes like the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ksatriyas 
}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 vai\'e7yas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 worship the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vi\'f1\'ebu-tattvas }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 generally.
\par Highly qualified }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'ebas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
situated in the mode of goodness have no grudges against the mode of worship of others. They have all respect for other demigods, even though they are ghastly looking, like the K\'e4la bhairava or Mah\'e4k\'e4l\'e9
, etc. They know very well that these horrible features of the Supreme Lord are all different servitors of the Lord under different conditions, yet they reject the worship of both horrible and attractive features of
 the demigods, and they concentrate only on the forms of Vi\'f1\'ebu because they are serious about liberation from the material conditions. The demigods, even to the stage of Brahm\'e4
, the supreme of all the demigods, cannot offer liberation to anyone. Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu underwent a severe type of penance to become eternal in life, but his worshipful deity, Brahm\'e4, could not satisfy him with such blessings. Therefore Vi\'f1\'eb
u is called }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 mukti-p\'e4da, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or the Personality of Godhead who can bestow upon us }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 mukti, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 liberation, and
 none else. The demigods, being like other living entities in the material world, are all liquidated at the time of the annihilation of the material structure. They are themselves unable to get liberation, and what to speak of giving liberation to their d
evotees. The demigods can award the worshipers some temporary benefit only and not the ultimate one.
\par It is for this reason only that candidates for liberation deliberately reject the worship of the demigods, although they have no disrespect for any one of them.
