\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12326592 {\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 In the revealed scriptures, the ultimate object of knowledge is \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, the Personality of Godhead. The purpose of performing sacrifice is to please Him. Yoga is for realizing Him. All fruitive activities are ultimately rewarded by Him only. He is supreme knowledge, and all severe auste
rities are performed to know Him. Religion [dharma] is rendering loving service unto Him. He is the supreme goal of life.
\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10492968 
\par }\pard \qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10492968 {\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 PURPORT
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12326592 {\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 That \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the Personality of Godhead, is the only object of worship is confirmed in these two }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7lokas. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
In the Vedic literature there is the same objective: establishing one's relationship and ultimately reviving our lost loving service unto Him. That is the sum and substance of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas. }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 In the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 the same theory is confirmed by the Lord in His 
own words: the ultimate purpose of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
is to know Him only. All the revealed scriptures are prepared by the Lord through His incarnation in the body of \'c7r\'e9la Vy\'e4sadeva just to remind the fallen souls conditioned by material nature of \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba the Pe
rsonality of Godhead. No demigod can award freedom from material bondage. That is the verdict of all the Vedic literatures. Impersonalists who have no information of the Personality of Godhead minimize the omnipotency of the Supreme Lord and put Him on eq
ual footing with all other living beings, and for this act such impersonalists get freedom from material bondage with great difficulty. They can only surrender unto Him after many, many births and culture of transcendental knowledge.
\par One may argue that the Vedic activities are based on sacrificial ceremonies. That is true. But all such sacrifices are also meant for realizing the truth about V\'e4sudeva. Another name of V\'e4sudeva is Yaj\'efa (sacrifice), and in the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 it is clearly stated that all sacrifices and all activities are to be conducted for the satisfaction of Yaj\'efa or Vi\'f1\'eb
u the Personality of Godhead. This is the case also with the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 yoga }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 systems. }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Yoga }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 means to get into touch with the Supreme Lord. The process, however, includes several bodily features such as }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e4sana, dhy\'e4na, pr\'e4\'eb\'e4y\'e4ma, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 meditation, etc., and all of them are meant for concentrating upon the localized aspect of V\'e4sudeva represented as Param\'e4tm\'e4. Param\'e4tm\'e4 realization is but partial realization of V\'e4
sudeva, and if one is successful in that attempt, one realizes V\'e4sudeva in full. But by ill luck most of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 yog\'e9s }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
are stranded by the powers of mysticism achieved through the bodily process. Ill-fated }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 yog\'e9s }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
are given a chance in the next birth by being placed in the families of good learned }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'ebas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
or in the families of rich merchants in order to execute the unfinished task of V\'e4sudeva realization. If such fortunate }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'ebas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
and sons of rich men properly utilize the chance, they can easily realize V\'e4sudeva by good association with saintly
 persons. Unfortunately, such preferential persons are captivated again by material wealth and honor and practically forget the aim of life.
\par This is also so for the culture of knowledge. According to }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 there are eighteen items in culturing know
ledge. And by such culture of knowledge one becomes gradually prideless, devoid of vanity, nonviolent, forbearing, simple, devoted to the great spiritual master and self-controlled. By culture of knowledge one becomes unattached to hearth and home and bec
omes conscious of the miseries due to death, birth, old age and disease. And all culture of knowledge culminates in devotional service to the Personality of Godhead, V\'e4sudeva. Therefore, V\'e4
sudeva is the ultimate aim in culturing all different branches of knowledge. Culture of knowledge leading one to the transcendental plane of meeting V\'e4sudeva is real knowledge. Physical knowledge in its various branches is condemned in the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 as }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 aj\'ef\'e4na, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
or the opposite of real knowledge. The ultimate aim of phys
ical knowledge is to satisfy the senses, which means prolongation of the term of material existence and thereby continuance of the threefold miseries. So prolonging the miserable life of material existence is nescience. But the same physical knowledge lea
ding to the way of spiritual understanding helps one to end the miserable life of physical existence and to begin the life of spiritual existence on the plane of V\'e4sudeva.
\par The same applies to all kinds of austerities. }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Tapasya }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 means voluntary acceptance of bodily pains to achieve some higher end of life. R\'e4va\'eba and Hira
\'ebyaka\'e7ipu underwent a severe type of bodily torture to achieve the end of sense gratification. Sometimes modern politicians also undergo severe types of austerities to achieve some political end. This is not actually }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 tapasya. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 One should accept voluntary bodily inconvenience for the sake of knowing V\'e4
sudeva because that is the way of real austerities. Otherwise all forms of austerities are classified as modes of pas
sion and ignorance. Passion and ignorance cannot end the miseries of life. Only the mode of goodness can mitigate the threefold miseries of life. Vasudeva and Devak\'e9, the so-called father and mother of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, underwent penances to get V
\'e4sudeva as their son. Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a is the father of all living beings (Bg. 14.4). Therefore He is the original living being of all other living beings. He is the original eternal enjoyer amongst all other enjoyers. Therefore no one can be His begetting father, as the ignorant may think.

\par Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba agreed to become the son of Vasudeva and Devak\'e9 upon being pleased with their severe austerities. Therefore if any austerities have to be done, they must be done to achieve the end of knowledge, V\'e4sudeva.
\par V\'e4sudeva is the original Personality of Godhead Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. As explained before, the original Personality of Godhead expands Himself by innumerable forms. Such expansion of forms is made possible by His various energies. His energies are also multifarious, and His inte
rnal energies are superior and external energies are inferior in quality. They are explained in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 (Bg. 7.4-6) as the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 par\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 apar\'e4 prak\'e5tis. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
So His expansions of various forms which take place via the internal energies are superior forms, 
whereas the expansions which take place via the external energies are inferior forms. The living entities are also His expansions. The living entities who are expanded by His internal potency are eternally liberated persons, whereas those who are expanded
 
by the material energies are eternally conditioned souls. Therefore, all culture of knowledge, austerities, sacrifice and activities should be aimed at changing the quality of the influence that is acting upon us. For the present, we are all being control
led by the external energy of the Lord, and just to change the quality of the influence, we must endeavor to cultivate spiritual energy. In the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 it is said that those who are }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 mah\'e4tm\'e4s, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or those whose minds have been so broadened as to be engage
d in the service of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, are under the influence of the internal potency, and the effect is that such broad-minded living beings are constantly engaged in the service of the Lord without deviation. That should be the aim of life. And that is the ver
dict of all the Vedic literatures. No one should bother himself with fruitive activities or dry speculation about transcendental knowledge. Everyone should at once engage himself in the transcendental loving service of the Lord. Nor should one worship dif
f
erent demigods who work as different hands of the Lord for creation, maintenance or destruction of the material world. There are innumerable powerful demigods who look over the external management of the material world. They are all different assisting ha
nds of Lord V\'e4sudeva. Even Lord \'c7iva and Lord Brahm\'e4 are included within the list of demigods, but Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu or V\'e4
sudeva is always transcendentally situated. Even though He accepts the quality of goodness of the material world, He is still transcendental t
o all the material modes. The following example will clear that matter more explicitly. In the prison house there are the prisoners and the managers of the prison house. Both the managers and the prisoners are bound up by the laws of the king. But even th
ough the king sometimes comes in the prison, he is not bound by the laws of the prison house. The king is therefore always transcendental to the laws of the prison house, as the Lord is always transcendental to the laws of the material world.
\par }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
