nted a stair case to be built up directly reaching the heavenly planet so that people might not be required to undergo the routine of pious work necessary to enter that planet. He also wanted to perform other acts against the established rule of the Lord.
 He even challenged the authority of \'c7r\'e9 R\'e4ma the Personality of Godhead and kidnapped His wife S\'e9t\'e4. Of course Lord R\'e4
ma came to chastise this atheist, answering the prayer and desire of the demigods. He therefore took up the challenge of R\'e4va\'eba, and the complete activity is the subject matter of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 R\'e4m\'e4ya
\'eba. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Because Lord R\'e4macandra was the Personality of Godhead, He exhibited superhuman activities which no human being, including the materially advanced R\'e4va\'eba, could perform. Lord R\'e4
