\par }\pard \qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16667501 {\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 PURPORT
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12326592 {\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 The prompt diagnosis of \'c7r\'e9 N\'e4rada is at once declared. The root cause of the despondency of Vy\'e4
sadeva was his deliberate avoidance of glorifying the Lord in his various editions of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Pur\'e4\'ebas. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
He has certainly, as a matter of course, given descriptions of the glories of the Lord (\'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba) but not as many as given to religiosity, economic development, sense gratification and salvation.
 These four items are by far inferior to engagement in the devotional service of the Lord. \'c7r\'e9 Vy\'e4
sadeva as the authorized scholar knew very well this difference. And still instead of giving more importance to the better type of engagement, namely, the dev
otional service to the Lord, he had more or less improperly used his valuable time, and thus he was despondent. From this it is clearly indicated that no one can be pleased substantially without being engaged in the devotional service of the Lord. In the 
}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 this fact is clearly mentioned.
\par After liberation, which is the last item in the line of performing religiosity, etc., one is engaged in pure devotional service. This is called the stage of self-realization or }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 brahma-bh\'fcta }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 stage. After attainment of this }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 brahma-bh\'fcta }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
stage, one is satisfied. But satisfaction is the beginning of transcendental bliss. One should progress by attaining neutrality and equality in the relative world. And passing this stage of equanimity, one is fixed up in the transce
ndental loving service of the Lord. This is the instruction of the Personality of Godhead in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
The conclusion is that in order to maintain the status quo of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 brahma-bh\'fcta }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 stage, as also to increase the degree of transcendental realizati
on, it is recommended by N\'e4rada to Vy\'e4sadeva that he (Vy\'e4sadeva) should now eagerly and repeatedly describe the path of devotional service. This would cure him from gross despondency.
\par }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
