\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12326592 {\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 A devotee of the Lord automatically becomes uninterested in the enchantment of material existence because he is }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 rasa-graha, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or one who has tasted the sweetness of the lotus feet of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. There are certainly many instances where devotees of the Lord have fallen down due to uncongenial association, just like fruitive workers, who are always prone to de
gradation. But even though he falls down, a devotee is never to be considered the same as a fallen }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 karmi. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 A }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 karmi }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 suffers the result of his own fruitive reactions, whereas a devotee is reformed by chastisement directed by the Lord Himself. The sufferings o
f an orphan and the sufferings of a beloved child of a king are not one and the same. An orphan is really poor because he has no one to take care of him, but a beloved son of a rich man, although he appears to be on the same level as the orphan, is always
 
under the vigilance of his capable father. A devotee of the Lord, due to wrong association, sometimes imitates the fruitive workers. The fruitive workers want to lord it over the material world. Similarly, a neophyte devotee foolishly thinks of accumulati
n
g some material power in exchange for devotional service. Such foolish devotees are sometimes put into difficulty by the Lord Himself. As a special favor, He may remove all material paraphernalia. By such action, the bewildered devotee is forsaken by all 
friends and relatives, and so he comes to his senses again by the mercy of the Lord and is set right to execute his devotional service.
\par In the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 it is also said that such fallen devotees are given a chance to take birth in a family of highly qualified }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'ebas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
or in a rich mercantile family. A devotee in such a position is not as fortunate as one who is chastised by the Lord and put into a position seemingly of helplessness. The devotee who becomes helpless by the will of the Lord is more fortun
ate than those who are born in good families. The fallen devotees born in a good family may forget the lotus feet of the Lord because they are less fortunate, but the devotee who is put into a forlorn condition is more fortunate because he swiftly returns
 to the lotus feet of the Lord, thinking himself helpless all round.
\par Pure devotional service is so spiritually relishable that a devotee becomes automatically uninterested in material enjoyment. That is the sign of perfection in progressive devotional service. A pure devotee continuously remembers the lotus feet of Lord 
\'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba and does not forget Him even for a moment, not even in exchange for all the opulence of the three worlds.
\par 
