\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12326592 {\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Lord \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu explained this }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e4tm\'e4r\'e4ma \'e7loka }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 very vividly before His chief devotee \'c7r\'e9la San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9. He points out eleven factors in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7loka, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 namely 1) }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e4tm\'e4r\'e4ma, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 2) }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 munaya\'f9, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 3) }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 nirgrantha, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 4) }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 api, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 5) }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ca, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 6) }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 urukrama, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid7831397 7)}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  kurvanti, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 8) }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ahaituk\'e9m, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 9) }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 bhaktim, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 10) }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ittham-bh\'fcta-gu\'eba\'f9, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and 11) }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 hari\'f9. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 According to the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vi\'e7va-Prak\'e4\'e7
a Sanskrit Dictionary, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 there are seven synonyms for the word }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e4tm\'e4r\'e4ma, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 which are as follows: 1) }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1186441\charrsid1186441 Brahman}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  (the Absolute Truth), 2) body, 3) mind, 4) endeavor, 5) endurance, 6) intelligence, and 7) personal habits.
\par The word }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 munaya\'f9 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 refers to 1) those who are thoughtful, 2) those who are grave or silent, 3) ascetics, 4) the persistent, 5) mendicant
s, 6) sages, and 7) saints.
\par The word }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 nirgrantha }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
conveys these ideas: 1) one who is liberated from nescience, 2) one who has no connection with scriptural injunction, i.e., who is freed from the obligation of the rules and regulations mentioned in the revealed scriptures like ethics, }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
philosophy, psychology, metaphysics, etc., (in other words the fools, illiterate, urchins, etc., who have no connection with regulative principles), 3) a capitalist, and also 4) one who is penniless.
\par According to the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7abda-ko\'e7a Dictionary, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 the affix }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ni }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
is used in the sense of 1) certainty, 2) counting, 3) building, and 4) forbiddance, and the word }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 grantha }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
is used in the sense of wealth, thesis, vocabulary, etc.
\par The word }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 urukrama }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 means the one whose activities are glorious. }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Krama }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 means step. This word }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 urukrama }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 specifically indicates the Lord's incarnation as V\'e4
mana, who covered the whole universe by immeasurable steps. Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is powerful, and His activities are so glorious that He has created the spiritual world by Hi
s internal potency and the material world by His external potency. By His all-pervading features He is everywhere present as the Supreme Truth, and in His personal feature He is always present in His transcendental abode of Goloka V\'e5nd\'e4
vana where He displays His transcendental pastimes in all variegatedness. His activities cannot be compared with anyone else's, and therefore the word }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 urukrama }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is just applicable to Him only.
\par According to Sanskrit verbal arrangement, }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 kurvanti }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 means to do things for someone else. Therefore, it means that the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e4tm\'e4r\'e4mas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 render devotional service unto the Lord not for personal interest but for the pleasure of the Lord, Urukrama.
\par }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid7831397     }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Hetu }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 means causal. There are many causes for one's sense satisfaction, and they can be chiefly clas
sified as material enjoyment, mystic powers and liberation, which are generally desired by progressive persons. As far as material enjoyments are concerned, they are innumerable, and the materialists are eager to increase them more and more because they a
r
e under the illusory energy. There is no end to the list of material enjoyments, nor can anyone in the material universe have all of them. As far as the mystic powers are concerned, they are eight in all (such as to become the minutist in form, to become 
weightless, to have anything one desires, to lord it over the material nature, to control other living beings, to throw earthly globes in outer space, etc.). These mystic powers are mentioned in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bh\'e4
gavatam }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 (11.15). The forms of liberation are five in number.
\par Therefore, unalloyed devotion means service to the Lord without desire for the above-mentioned personal benefits. And the powerful Personality of Godhead \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba can be fully satisfied by such unalloye
d devotees free from all sorts of desires for personal benefit.
\par Unalloyed devotional service of the Lord progresses in different stages. Practice of devotional service in the material field is of eighty-one different qualities, and above such activities th
ere is the transcendental practice of devotional service, which is one and is called }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 s\'e4dhana-bhakti. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 When unalloyed practice of }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 s\'e4dhana-bhakti }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is matured into transcendental love for the Lord, the transcendental loving service of the Lord begins gradually 
developing into nine progressive stages of loving service under the headings of attachment, love, affection, feelings, affinity, adherence, following, ecstasy and intense feelings of separation.
\par The attachment of an inactive devotee develops up to the stag
e of transcendental love of God. Attachment of an active servitor develops up to the stage of adherence, and that for a friendly devotee develops up to the stage of following, and the same is also the case for the paternal devotees. Devotees in conjugal l
ove develop ecstasy up to the stage of intense feelings of separation. These are some of the features of unalloyed devotional service of the Lord.
\par According to }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Hari-bhakti-sudhodaya, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 the import of the word }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ittham-bh\'fcta }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is complete bliss. Transcendental bliss in the realization of impersonal }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1186441\charrsid1186441 Brahman}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
 becomes comparable with the scanty water contained in the pit made by a cow's hoof. It is nothing compared to the ocean of bliss of the vision of the Personality of Godhead. The personal form of Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba is 
so attractive that it comprehends all attraction, all bliss and all tastes }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 (rasas). }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 These attractions are so strong that }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 no one wants to exchange material enjoyment, mystic powers and liberation for them. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 There is no need of logical arguments in support of
 this statement, but out of one's own nature one becomes attracted by the qualities of Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. We must know for certain that the qualities of the Lord have nothing to do with mundane qualities. All of them are full of bliss, knowledge and eternity.
 There are innumerable qualities of the Lord, and one is attracted by one quality while another is attracted by another.
\par Great sages, such as the four bachelor devotees Sanaka, San\'e4tana, Sanand}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid3436515 a and Sanat-k}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 um\'e4ra, are attracted by the fragrance of flowers and }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 tulas\'e9 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 leaves anointed with the pulp of sandalwood offered at the lotus feet of the Lord. Similarly, \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 was attracted by the transcendental pastimes of the Lord. \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 was already situated in the liberated stage, yet he was attr
acted by the pastimes of the Lord. This proves that the quality of His pastimes has nothing to do with material affinity. Similarly, the young cowherd damsels were attracted by the bodily feature of the Lord, and Rukmi\'eb\'e9
 was attracted by hearing about the glories of the Lord. Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a attracts even the mind of the goddess of fortune. He attracts, in special cases, the minds of all young girls. He attracts the minds of the elderly ladies by paternal affection. He attracts the minds of the male in the humor
s of servitude and friendship.
\par The word }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 hari }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
conveys various meanings, but the chief import of the word is that He (the Lord) vanquishes everything inauspicious and takes away the mind of the devotee by awarding pure transcendental love. By remembering the
 Lord in acute distress one can be free from all varieties of miseries and anxieties. Gradually the Lord vanquishes all obstacles on the path of devotional service of a pure devotee, and the result of nine devotional activities, such as hearing, chanting,
 etc., becomes manifested.
\par By His personal features and transcendental attributes, the Lord attracts all psychological activities of a pure devotee. Such is the attractive power of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. The attraction is so powerful that a pure devotee never hankers 
for any one of the four principles of religion. These are the attractive features of the transcendental attributes of the Lord. And adding to this the words }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 api }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ca, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 one can increase the imports unlimitedly. According to Sanskrit grammar there are seven }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid3436515 synonyms}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  for the word }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 api.
\par }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 So by interpreting each and every word of this }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7loka, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
one can see unlimited numbers of transcendental qualities of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba that attract the mind of a pure devotee.
\par }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
