\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12326592 {\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba had two arms, and why He is designated as four-armed is explained by \'c7r\'e9dhara Sv\'e4m\'e9. Both Bh
\'e9ma and Draupad\'e9 held opposite views about killing A\'e7vatth\'e4m\'e4. Bh\'e9ma wanted him to be immediately killed, whereas Draupad\'e9 wanted to save him. We can imagine Bh\'e9ma ready to kill while Draupad\'e9
 is obstructing him. And in order to prevent both of them, the Lord discovered another two arms. Originally, the primeval Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba displays only two arms, but in His N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba feature He exhibits four. In His N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a feature He resides with His devotees in the Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha planets, while in His original \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba feature He resides in the K\'e5\'f1\'ebaloka planet far, far above the Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha planets in the spiritual sky. Therefore, if \'c7r
\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba is called }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 caturbhuja\'f9, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 there is no contradiction. If need be He can display hundreds of arms, as He exhibited in His }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 vi\'e7va-r\'fcpa }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 shown to Arjuna. Therefore, one who can display hundreds and thousands of arms can also manifest four whenever needed.
\par When Arjuna was perplexed about what to do with A\'e7vatth\'e4m\'e4, Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba, as very dear friend of Arjuna, voluntarily took up the matter just to make a solution. And He was smiling also.
\par 
