a, as Garbhodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu, first of a
ll entered the material universe. Without spiritual contact, matter cannot create. This principle was followed from the very beginning of the creation. The Supreme Spirit entered the universe, and the first living being, Brahm\'e4
, was born on a lotus flower grown out of the transcendental abdomen of Vi\'f1\'ebu. Vi\'f1\'ebu is therefore known as Padman}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid6712803 a}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 bha. Brahm\'e4 is known as }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e4tma-bh\'fc }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 because he was begotten directly from the father without any contact of mother Lak\'f1m\'e9j\'e9. Lak\'f1m\'e9j\'e9 was present just before N
\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, engaged in the service of the Lord, and still, without contact with Lak\'f1m\'e9j\'e9, N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba begot Brahm\'e4. That is the omnipotcncy of the Lord. One who foolishly considers N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a like other living beings should take a lesson from this. N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba is not an ordinary li
ving being. He is the Personality of Godhead Himself, and He has all the potencies of all the senses in all parts of His transcendental body. An ordinary living being begets a child by the intercourse of sex, and he has no other means to beget a child oth
er than the one designed for him. But N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, being omnipotent, is not bound to any condition of energy. He is complete and independent to do anything and everything by His various potencies, very easily and perfectly. Brahm\'e4
 is therefore directly the son of the father and was not put into the womb of a mother. Therefore he is known as}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  \'e4tma-bh\'fc. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 This Brahm\'e4
 is in charge of further creations in the universe, secondarily reflected by the potency of the Omnipotent. Within the halo of the universe there is a transcendental planet known as \'c7vetadv\'e9pa, which is the abode of the K\'f1\'e9rodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9
 Vi\'f1\'ebu, the Param\'e4tm\'e4 feature of the Supreme Lord. When ever there is trouble in the universe that cannot be solved by the administrative demigods, they approach Brahm\'e4j\'e9 for a solution, and if it is not to be solved even by Brahm\'e4j
\'e9 then Brahm\'e4j\'e9 consults and prays to the K\'f1\'e9rodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu for an incarnation and solution to the problems. Such a problem arose when Ka\'e0sa and others were ruling over the earth and the earth beca
me too much overburdened by the misdeeds of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 asuras. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Brahm\'e4j\'e9, along with other demigods, prayed at the shore of the K\'f1\'e9
rodaka Ocean, and they were advised of the descent of K\'e5\'f1\'eba as the son of Vasudeva and Devak\'e9. So some people say that the Lord appeared because of the prayers of Brahm\'e4j\'e9.
