\par The opposite tendency is the cause of falldown. The living entity has this tendency of falling down by dint of misidentifying him
self as fully independent to lord it over the material world. The root cause of all troubles is there in false egoism. One must draw towards the Lord in all circumstances.
\par The appearance of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba at the deathbed of Bh\'e9\'f1maj\'e9 is due to his being an unflinching devotee of the Lord. Arjuna had some bodily relation with K\'e5\'f1\'eba because the Lord happened to be his maternal cousin. But Bh\'e9\'f1
ma had no such bodily relation. Therefore the cause of attraction was due to the intimate relation of the soul. Yet because the relation of the body is very pleasing and natural, the Lord is more pleased when He is addressed as the son of Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Nanda, the son of Ya\'e7od\'e4, the lover of R\'e4dh\'e4r\'e4\'eb\'e9. This affinity by bodily relation with the Lord is another feature of reciprocating loving service to the Lord. Bh\'e9\'f1
madeva is conscious of this sweetness of transcendental humor, and therefore he likes to address the Lord as }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vijaya Sakhe, P\'e4rtha Sakhe, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
