\par The }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
is prescribed for the civilized human being just to train him to successfully terminate human life. Self-realization is distinguished from the life of the lower animals engaged in eating, sleeping, fearing and mating. Bh\'e9\'f1
madeva advised for all human beings nine qualifications: 1) not to become angry, 2) not to lie, 3) to equally distribute wealth, 4) to forgive, 5) to beget children only by one's legitimate wife. 6) to be pure in mind and hygeni
c in body. 7) not to be inimical toward anyone, 8) to be simple, and 9) to support servants or subordinates. One cannot be called a civilized person without acquiring the above-mentioned preliminary qualities. Besides these, the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'ebas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or the intelligen
t men, the administrative men, the mercantile community and the laborer class must acquire special qualities in terms of occupational duties mentioned in all the Vedic scriptures. For the intelligent men, controlling the senses is the most essential quali
f
ication, which is the basis of morality. Sex indulgence even with a legitimate wife must also be controlled, and thereby family control will automatically follow. An intelligent man abuses his great qualifications if he does not follow the Vedic way of li
fe. This means he must seriously make a study of the Yedic literatures, especially of the }{\i\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
For learning Vedic knowledge, one must approach a person who is cent percent engaged in devotional service. He must not do things which are forbidden in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7\'e4stras. }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
A person cannot be a teacher if he drinks or smokes. In the modern system of education the teacher's academic qualification is taken into consideration without evaluation of his moral life. Therefore, the result of e
ducation is misuse of high intelligence in so many ways.
\par The }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 k\'f1atriyas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or the administrative class is especially advised to give in charity }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
and not to accept charity in any circumstances. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Modern administrators raise subscriptions for some political functio
ns, but never give in charity to the citizens in any state function. It is just the reverse in the injunctions of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e7\'e4stras. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
