\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bh\'e9\'f1
madeva is a great devotee of the Lord in the relation of servitorship. Thus his throwing of sharp arrows at the transcendental body of the Lord is as good as the worship of another devotee who throws soft roses upon Him.
\par It appears that Bh\'e9\'f1madeva is repen
ting his actions, which he committed against the person of the Lord. But factually the Lord's body was not at all pained due to His transcendental existence. His body is not matter. Both He Himself and His body are complete spiritual identity. Spirit is n
ever pierced, burnt, dried, moistened, etc. This is vividly explained in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 So also it is stated in-the }{
