are eternally liberated souls, and they are eternally engaged in the reciprocation of transcendental loving service with the Lord in His eternal abode beyond the manifested mundane creations. But the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
nitya-baddha }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 or eternally conditioned souls are entrusted to His external energy, }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 m\'e4y\'e4, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
for rectification of their rebellious attitude towards the Supreme Father. }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Nitya-baddhas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 are eternally forgetful of their relation with the Lord as parts
 and parcels. They are bewildered by the illusory energy as products of matter, and thus they are very busy in making plans in the material world for becoming happy. They go on merrily with plans, but by the will of the Lord both the planmakers and the pl
ans are annihilated at the end of a certain period, as above mentioned. This is confirmed in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 as follows: "O son of Kunt\'e9
