\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 He is self-sufficient, and there is no need for Him to seek happiness from anything beyond Himself. He is self-sufficient because His v
ery transcendental existence is total bliss. He is eternally existent; He is all-cognizant and all-blissful. Therefore, any presentation, however valuable it may be, is not needed by Him. But still, because He is the well-wisher for one and all, He accept
s
 from everyone everything that is offered to Him in pure devotional service. It is not that He is in want for such things because the things are themselves generated from His energy. The comparison is made herein that it is something like offering a lamp 
in the worship of the sun-god. Anything fiery and illuminating is but an emanation of the energy of the sun, and yet to worship the sun-god it is necessary to offer him a lamp.
\par In the worship of the sun, there is some sort of demand made by the worshiper, b
ut in the case of devotional service of the Lord, there is no question of demand from either side. It is all a sign of pure love and affection between the Lord and the devotee.
\par The Lord is the Supreme Father of all living beings, and therefore those who are conscious of this }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 vital }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
relation with God can make filial demands from the Father, and the Father is pleased to supply the demands of such obedient sons without bargaining. The Lord is just like the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 desire tree, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and from Him everyone can have everything 
by the causeless mercy of the Lord. As the Supreme Father, the Lord, however, does not supply to a pure devotee what is considered to be a barrier to the discharge of devotional service. Those who are engaged in the devotional service of the Lord can rise
