alia of the modern metropolis. The propensity to utilize nature's own gifts is still there, even in the heart of modern civilized men. The leaders of modern civilization select their own residential quarters in a place where there are such naturally beaut
iful gardens and reservoirs of water, but they leave the common men to reside in congested areas with out parks and gardens. Herein of course we find a different description of the city of Dv\'e4rak\'e4. It is understood that the whole }{
