\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12326592 {\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid9968813\charrsid15938164     }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid15938164 Vasudeva:}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 {\*\bkmkstart here4}
{\*\bkmkend here4} }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Son of King \'c7\'fcrasena, husband of Devak\'e9 and father of Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba. He is the brother of Kunt\'e9 and father of Subhadr\'e4. Subhadr\'e4
 was married with her cousin Arjuna, and this system is still prevalent in some parts of India. Vasudeva was appointed minister of Ugrasena, and later on he married eight daughters of Ugrasena's brother Devaka. Devak\'e9 is only one of them. Ka\'e0
sa was his brother-in-law, and Vasudeva accepted voluntary imprisonment by Ka\'e0sa on mutual agreement to deliver the eighth son of Devak\'e9. This was foiled by the will of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. As maternal uncle of the P\'e4\'eb\'f2
avas, he took active parts in the purificatory process of the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas. He sent for the priest Ka\'e7yapa at the \'c7atas\'e5\'ecga Parvata, and he executed the functions. When K\'e5\'f1\'eba appeared within the bars of Ka\'e0
sa's prison house, He was transferred to Gokula by Vasudeva at the house of Nanda Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, the foster father of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. K\'e5\'f1\'eba disappeared along with Baladeva prior to the disappearance of Vasudeva, a
nd Arjuna (his nephew) undertook the charge of the funeral ceremony after his disappearance.
\par }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid9968813     }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Akr\'fcra: }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 The commander-in-chief of the V\'e5\'f1\'ebi dynasty and a great devotee of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Akr\'fc
ra attained success in devotional service of the Lord by the one single process of offering prayers. He was the husband of S\'fctan\'e9, daughter of Ah\'fcka. He supported Arjuna when Arjuna took Subhadr\'e4 forcibly away by the will of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. Both K\'e5\'f1\'eba and Akr\'fcra went to see Arjuna after his successful kidnapping of Subhadr\'e4. Both of them presented dowries to Arjuna after this incidence. Akr\'fcra was present also when Abhimanyu, the son of Subhadr\'e4
, was married with Uttar\'e4, mother of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it. Ah\'fcka, the father-in-law of Akr\'fcra, was not on good terms with Akr\'fcra. But both of them were devotees of the Lord.
\par }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid9968813     }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Ugrasena: }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 One of the powerful kings of the V\'e5\'f1\'ebi dynasty and cousin of Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Kuntibhoja. His other name is Ah\'fcka. His minister was V}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid9968813 a}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sudeva, and}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
his son was the powerful Ka\'e0sa. This Ka\'e0sa imprisoned his father and became the King of Mathur\'e4. By the grace of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba and His brother Lord Baladeva, Ka\'e0sa was killed, and Ugrasena was reinstalled on the throne. When \'c7\'e4lva}
{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 attacked the city of Dv\'e4rak\'e4, Ugrasena fought very valiantly and repulsed the enemy. Ugrasena inquired from N\'e4radaj\'e9 about the divinity of Lord K
\'e5\'f1\'eba. When the Yadu dynasty was to be vanquished, Ugrasena was entrusted with the iron lump produced from the womb of S\'e4mba. He cut the iron lump into pieces and then pasted it and mixed it up with the sea water on the coast of Dv\'e4rak\'e4
. After this, he ordered complete prohibition within the city of Dv\'e4rak\'e4 and the kingdom. He got salvation after his death.
\par }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592     }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid15938164 Baladeva: }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid15938164 He}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
 is the divine son of Vasudeva by his wife Rohi\'eb\'e9. He is also known as Rohi\'eb\'e9nandana, the beloved son of Rohi\'eb\'e9. He was also entrusted to Nanda Mah\'e4r\'e4ja along with His mother Rohi\'eb\'e9
 when Vasudeva embraced imprisonment by mutual agreement with Ka\'e0sa. So Nanda Mah\'e4r\'e4ja is also the foster father of Baladeva along with Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba and Lord 
Baladeva both were constant companions from very childhood, although They were stepbrothers. He is the plenary manifestation of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and therefore He is as good and powerful as Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. He belongs to the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vi\'f1\'ebu-tattva }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 (the principle of Godhead). He attended the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 svaya\'e0vara }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ceremony of Draupad\'e9 along with \'c7r\'e9}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 K\'e5\'f1\'eba. When Subhadr\'e4
 was kidnapped by Arjuna by the organized plan of \'c7r\'e9}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Baladeva was very angry with Arjuna and wanted to kill him at once. \'c7r\'e9}{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 K\'e5\'f1\'eba, for the sake of His dear friend, fell at the feet of Lord Baladeva and implored Him not to be so angry. \'c7r\'e9
 Baladeva was thus satisfied. Similarly, He was once very angry with the Kauravas, and He wanted to throw the whole city into the depths of the Yamun\'e4
. But the Kauravas satisfied him by surrendering unto His divine lotus feet. He was actually the seventh son of Devak\'e9 prior to the birth of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, but by the will of the Lord He was transferred to the womb of Rohi\'eb\'e9
 to escape the wrath of Ka\'e0sa. His other name is therefore Sa\'eckar\'f1a\'eba}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 , }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 who is also the plenary portion of \'c7r\'e9}{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Baladeva. Because He was as powerful as Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba and can bestow spiritual power to the devotees, He is therefore known as Baladeva. In the }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Vedas }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 also it is enjoined that no one can know the Supreme Lord without being favored by Baladeva. }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bala }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 means spiritual strength and not physical. Some less intelligent persons interpret }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 bala }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
as the strength of the body. But no one can have spiritual realization by physical strength. Physical strength ends with the end of the physical body, but spiritual strength follows the spirit soul to the next transmigration}{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 , }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 and therefore the strength obtained by Baladeva is never wasted.
\par The strength is eternal, and thus Baladeva is the original spiritual master of all devotees.
\par \'c7r\'e9 Baladeva was also a class friend of Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba as a student of S\'e4nd\'e9pani }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid16606422\charrsid16606422 Muni}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 . In His childhood He killed many }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 asuras }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 along with \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and specifically He killed the Dhenuk\'e4sura at T\'e4lavana. During the Kuruk\'f1etra ba
ttle, He remained neutral, and He tried his best not to bring about the fight. He was in favor of Duryodhana, but still He remained neutral. When there was a club-fight between Duryodhana and Bh\'e9masena, He was present on the spot. He was angry at Bh
\'e9masena when the latter struck Duryodhana on the thigh or below the belt, and He wanted to retaliate the unfair action. Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba saved Bh\'e9ma from His wrath. But He left the place at once, being disgusted at Bh\'e9
masena, and after His departure Duryodhana fell to the ground to meet his death. The funeral ceremony of Abhimanyu, the son of Arjuna, was performed by Him, as He was the maternal uncle. It was impossible to be performed by any one of the P\'e4\'eb\'f2
avas, who were all overwhelmed with grief. At the last stage, He departed from this world by producing a great white snake from His mouth, and thus He was carried by \'c7e\'f1an\'e4ga in the shape of a serpent.
\par }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592     Pradyumna: }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Incarnation of K\'e4madeva or, according to others, incarnation of }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid15938164 Sanat-kum\'e4ra}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 , born as the son of the Personality of Godhead Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba and Lak\'f1m\'e9dev\'e9 \'c7r\'e9mat\'e9 Rukmi\'eb\'e9, the principal queen at Dv\'e4rak\'e4
. He was one of those who went to congratulate Arjuna upon marrying Subhadr\'e4. He was one of the great generals who fought with \'c7\'e4lva, and while fighting w
ith him he became unconscious on the battlefield. His charioteer brought him back to the camp from the battlefield, and for this action he was very sorry and rebuked his charioteer. However, he fought again with \'c7\'e4
lva and was victorious. He heard all about the different demigods from N\'e4radaj\'e9. He is one of the four plenary expansions of Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba. He is the third one. He inquired from his father \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a about the glories of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'ebas. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 During the fratricidal war amongst the descendants of Yadu, he died at the hand of Bhoja, another king of the V
\'e5\'f1\'ebis. After his death, he was installed in his original position.
\par }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid15938164     }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 C\'e4rude\'f1\'eba: }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Another son of Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba and Rukmi\'eb\'e9dev\'e9
. He was also present during the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 svaya\'e0vara }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ceremony of Draupad\'e9. He was a great
 warrior like his brothers and father. He fought with Vivindhaka and killed him in the fight.
\par }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid15938164     }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 S\'e4mba: }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 One of the great heroes of the Yadu dynasty and the son of Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba by His wife J\'e4
mbavat\'e9. He learned the military art of throwing arrows from Arjuna, and he became a member of parliament during the time of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira. He was present during the }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid15938164 R\'e4jas\'fcya-yaj\'efa}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira. When all the V\'e5\'f1\'ebis were assemb}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid15938164 led during the time of Prava\'e7a-y}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 aj\'ef
a, his glorious activities were narrated by S\'e4tyaki before Lord Baladeva. He was also present along with his father Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba during the A\'e7vamedha-}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid5327415 yaj\'efa}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  performed by Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira. He was presented before some }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e5\'f1is }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
falsely dressed as a pregnant woman by his brothers, and in fun he asked the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e5\'f1is }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 what he was going to deliver. The }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'e5\'f1is }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 replied that he would deliver a lump of iron, which would be the cause of fratricidal war in the family of Yadu. The next day, in the morning, S\'e4
mba delivered a large lump of iron, which was entrusted with Ugrasena for necessary action. Actually later on there was the foretold fratricidal war, and S\'e4mba died in that war.
\par So all these sons of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba left their respective palaces and leaving aside all engagements, including lying down, sitting and dining, hastened towards their exalted father.
