Conditioned living beings are always after the favor of the goddess of fortune, although by nature she is moving from one place to another. In the material world no one is permanently fortunate, however
 clever one may be. There have been so many big empires in different parts of the world, there have been so many powerful kings all over the world, and there have been so many fortunate men, but all of them have been liquidated gradually. This is the law 
of material nature. But spiritually it is different. According to }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid8868304 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 , }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid8868304 the Lord is served very respect}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 fully by hundreds and thousands of goddesses of fortune. They are always in a lonely place also with the Lord. But still the association of the 
Lord is so inspiringly newer and newer that they cannot quit the Lord for a moment, even though they are by nature very restless and are moving about. The spiritual relation with the Lord is so enlivening and resourceful that no one can leave the company 
of the Lord, once having taken shelter of it.
\par The living beings are by constitution feminine by nature. The male or enjoyer is the Lord, and all manifestations of His different potencies are feminine by nature. In the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4, }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 the living beings are designated as }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid8868304\charrsid12326592 par\'e4}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 -prak\'e5ti, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
or the superior potency. The material elements are }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 apar\'e4-prak\'e5ti, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
or inferior potency. Such potencies are always employed for the satisfaction of the employer or the enjoyer. The supreme enjoyer is the Lord Himself, as stated in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 (Bg. 5.29). The potencies, therefore, when engaged directly in the service of the Lord, revive the natural color, and thus there is no disparity in the relation of the potent and potency.
\par Generally people engaged in service are a
lways seeking some post under the government or the supreme enjoyer of the state. Since the Lord is the supreme enjoyer of everything in or outside the universe, it is happiness to be employed by Him. Once engaged in the supreme governmental service of th
e
