\par During his student life he was entrusted to study under the great professor Dro\'eb\'e4c\'e4rya, along with other P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas and the Kurus. But he excelled everyone by his studious intensity, and Dro\'eb\'e4c\'e4
rya was especially attracted by his disciplinary affection. Dro\'eb\'e4c\'e4
rya accepted him as a first grade scholar and loved heartily to bestow upon him all the blessings of military science. He was so ardent a student that he used to practice bowmanship even at night, and for all these reasons Professor Dro\'eb\'e4c\'e4
rya was determined to make him the topmost bowman of the world. He passed very brilliantly the examination in piercing the target, and Dro\'eb\'e4c\'e4rya was very pleased. Royal families at Ma}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid9926308 n}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ipur and Tripura are descendants of Babhruv\'e4hana. He saved Dro\'eb\'e4c\'e4rya from the attack of a crocodile, and the }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid9926308\charrsid9926308 \'c4c\'e4rya}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 , being pleased with him, rewarded him a weapon of the name Brahma\'e7ira. Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Drupada was inimical toward Dro\'eb\'e4c\'e4rya, and thus when he attacked the }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid9926308\charrsid9926308 \'c4c\'e4rya}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 , Arjuna got him arrested and brought him before Dro\'eb\'e4c\'e4rya. He besieged a city of the name Ahichhatra, belonging to Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Drupada, and after taking it over he gave it to Dro\'eb\'e4c\'e4rya. The confidential treatment of the weapon Brahma\'e7ira was explained to Arjuna, and Dro\'eb\'e4c\'e4rya was promised by Arjuna that he would use the weapon if necessary when he (Dro
\'eb\'e4c\'e4rya) personally became an enemy of Arjuna. By this, the }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid9926308\charrsid9926308 \'c4c\'e4rya}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  forecasted the future battle of Kuruk\'f1etra, in which Dro\'eb\'e4c\'e4
rya was on the opposite side. Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Drupada, although defeated by Arjuna on behalf of his professor Dro\'eb\'e4c\'e4rya, decided to hand over his daughter Draupad\'e9
 to his young combatant, but he was disappointed when he heard the false news of Arjuna's death in the fire of a lac-house intrigued by Duryodhana. He therefore arranged for Draupad\'e9's personal se
lection of a groom who could pierce the eye of a fish hanging on the ceiling. This trick was especially made because only Arjuna could do it, and he was successful in his desire to hand over his equally worthy daughter to Arjuna. His brothers were at that
 time living incognito under agreement with Duryodhana, and Arjuna and his brothers attended the meeting of Draupad\'e9's selection in the dress of }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'ebas. }{
