\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 K\'e5\'f1\'eba made a plan to help Arjuna to kidnap Subhadr\'e4, sister of \'c7r\'e9}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 K\'e5\'f1\'eba, because Baladeva was inclined to hand her over to Duryodhana. Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira also agreed with \'c7r\'e9}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and thus Subhadr\'e4 was taken by force by Arjuna and then married to him. Subhadr\'e4's son is Abhimanyu, the father of Par\'e9k\'f1it Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, the posthumous child. He satisfied the fire-god by setting fire to the Kh\'e4\'eb\'f2ava Forest, and thus the fire-god gave him one weapon. Indra was angry when fire was set in the Kh\'e4\'eb\'f2ava Forest, a
nd thus Indra, assisted by all other demigods, began fighting with Arjuna for his great challenge. They were defeated by Arjuna, and Indradeva returned to his heavenly kingdom. Arjuna also promised all protection to one May\'e4
sura, and the latter presented him one valuable conchshell celebrated as the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid1462714 Devadatta}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 . }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
