\par When Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira was disappointed in defeating the King of Magadha, Jar\'e4sandha, it was Arjuna only who gave King Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira all kinds of assurances, and thus Arjuna, Bh\'e9ma and Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a started for Magadha to kill Jar\'e4sandha. When he went out to bring all other kings of the world under the subjection of the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas, as was 
