from Kuvera, the treasurer of the heavenly kingdom. Indra wanted him to come to the heavenly kingdom, the Indraloka planet beyond the moon planet. In that planet he was cordially received by the local r
esidents, and he was awarded reception in the heavenly parliament of Indradeva. Then he met Indradeva, who not only presented him with his Vajra weapon, but also taught him the military and musical science as used in the heavenly planet. In one sense, Ind
ra is the real father of Arjuna, and therefore indirectly he wanted to entertain Arjuna with the famous society girl of heaven, Urva\'e7\'e9 the celebrated beauty. The society girls of heaven are lusty, and Urva\'e7\'e9
 was very eager to contact Arjuna, the strongest human being, and she met him in his room and expressed her desires. But Arjuna sustained his unimpeachable character by closing his eyes before Urva\'e7\'e9
 and addressing her as mother of the Kuru dynasty and placing her in the category of his mothers Kunt\'e9, M\'e4dr\'e9 and \'c7ac\'e9dev\'e9, wife of Indradeva. Disappointed, Urva\'e7\'e9
 cursed Arjuna and left. In the heavenly planet he also met the great celebrated ascetic Lomasa and prayed to him for the protection of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira.
\par When his inimical cousin Duryodhana was under the clutches of the Gandharvas, he wanted to save him and requested the Gandharvas to release Duryodhana, but the Gandharvas refused, and thus he fought with them and got Duryodhana released. When all the P
\'e4\'eb\'f2avas lived incognito, he presented himself in the court of King Vir\'e4\'f6}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1462714 a}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  as a eunuch and was employed as the musical teacher of Uttar\'e4
, his future daughter-in-law, and was known in the Vir\'e4\'f6}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1462714 a}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  court as the B\'e5hannala. As B\'e5hannala, he fought on behalf of Uttar}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1462714 a}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 , the son of King Vir\'e4\'f6}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1462714 a}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 , and thus defeate
d the Kurus in the fight incognito. His secret weapons were safely kept in the custody of a }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 somi }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 tree, and he ordered Uttar}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1462714 a}{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  to get them back. His identity and his brothers' identity were later on disclosed to Uttar}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid1462714 a}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 . Dro\'eb\'e4c\'e4
rya was informed of Arjuna's presence in the fight of the Kurus and the Vir\'e4\'f6as. Later, on the Battlefield of Kuruk\'f1etra, Arjuna killed many great generals like Kar\'eba and others. After the Battle of Kuruk\'f1etra, he punished A\'e7vatth\'e4m
\'e4, who killed all the five sons of Draupad\'e9. Then all the brothers went to Bh\'e9\'f1madeva.
\par It is due to Arjuna only that the great philosophical discourses of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 were again spoken by the Lord on the Battlefield of Kuruk\'f1
etra. His wonderful acts on the Battlefield of Kuruk\'f1etra are vividly described in the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Mah\'e4bh\'e4rata. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Arjuna was, however, defeated by his son Babhruv
\'e4hana at Ma\'ebipura and fell unconscious when Ul\'fcp\'e9 saved him. After the disappearance of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the message was brought by him to Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira. Again, he visited Dv\'e4rak\'e4, and all the widow wives of Lord K
\'e5\'f1\'eba lamented before him. He took them all in the presence of Vasudeva and pacified all of them. Later on, when Vasudeva passed away, he performed his funeral ceremony in the absence of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. While Arjuna was taking all the wives of K
\'e5\'f1\'eba to Indraprastha, he was attacked on the way, and he could not protect the ladies in his custody. At last, advised by Vy\'e4sadeva, all the brothers headed for Mah\'e4
prasthan. On the way, at the request of his brother, he gave up all important weapons as useless, and he dropped them all in the water.
