\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1790059 {\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592     G\'e4ndh\'e4r\'e9: }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 The ideal c
haste lady in the history of the world. She was the daughter of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Subala, the King of G\'e4ndh\'e4ra (now Kandahar in Kabul), and in her maiden state she worshiped Lord \'c7iva. Lord \'c7
iva is worshiped generally by the Hindu maidens to get a good husband.
\par G\'e4ndh\'e4r\'e9 satisfied Lord \'c7iva, and by his benediction to obtain one hundred sons, she was betrothed to Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6ra, despite his being blind forever. When G\'e4ndh\'e4r\'e9
 came to know that her would-be husband was a blind man, to follow her life companion she decided to become voluntarily blind. So she wrapped up her eyes with many silk linens, and she was married to Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6
ra under the guidance of her elder brother \'c7akuni. She was the most beautiful girl of her time, and she was equally qualified by her womanly qual
ities, which endeared every member of the Kaurava court. But despite all her good qualities, she had the natural frailties of a woman, and she was envious of Kunt\'e9 when the latter gave birth to a male child. Both the queens were pregnant, but Kunt\'e9
 first gave birth to a male child. Thus G\'e4ndh\'e4r\'e9 became angry and gave a blow to her own abdomen. As a result, she gave birth to a lump of flesh only, but since she was a devotee of Vy\'e4sadeva, by instruction of Vy\'e4
sadeva the lump was divided into one hundred parts
, and each part gradually developed to become a male child. Thus her ambition to become the mother of one hundred sons was fulfilled, and she began to nourish all the children according to her exalted position. When the intrigue of the battlefield of Kuru
k\'f1etra was going on, she was not in favor of fighting with the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas; rather, she blamed Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6ra, her husband, for such a fratricidal war. She desired that the state be divided into two parts, for the sons of P\'e4\'eb\'f2
u and her own. She was very affected when all her sons died in the Battle of Kuruk\'f1etra, and she wanted to curse Bh\'e9masena and Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira, but she was checked by Vy\'e4sadeva. Her mourning over the death of Duryodhana and Du\'f9\'e7\'e4
sana before Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba is very pitiful, and Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba pacified her by transcendental messages. She was equally aggrieved on the death of Kar\'eba, and she described to Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba the lamentation of Kar\'eba\rquote 
s wife. She was pacified by \'c7r\'e9la Vy\'e4sadeva when he showed her dead sons, then promoted to the heavenly kingdoms. She died along with her husband in the jungles of the Himalayas near the mouth of the Ganges; she burned in a forest fire. Mah\'e4r
\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira performed the death ceremony of his uncle and aunt.
\par }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid15290236     }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 P\'e5th\'e4: }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Daughter of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja \'c7\'fcrasen}{\f35\fs28\insrsid15290236 a}{
\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  and sister of Vasudeva, Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba\rquote s father. Later she was adopted by Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Kuntibhoja, and hence she is known as Kunt\'e9
. She is the incarnation of the success potency of the Personality of Godhead. The heavenly denizens from the upper planets used to visit the palace of the King Kuntibhoja, and Kunt\'e9
 was engaged for their reception. She also served the great mystic sage Durv\'e4s\'e4, and being satisfied by her faithful service, Durv\'e4s\'e4 }{\f35\fs28\insrsid16606422\charrsid16606422 Muni}{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  gave her a }{
\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 mantra }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 by which it was possible for her to call for any d
emigod she pleased. As a matter of inquisitiveness, she at once called for the sun-god, who desired couplement with her, but she declined. But the sun-god assured her immunity from virgin adulteration, and so she agreed to his proposal. As a result of thi
s couplement, she became pregnant, and Kar\'eba was born by her. By the grace of the sun, she again turned into a virgin girl, but being afraid of her parents, she quitted the newly born child Kar\'eb
a. After that, when she actually selected her own husband, she preferred P\'e4\'eb\'f2u to be her husband. Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e4\'eb\'f2u later on wanted to retire from family life and adopt the renounced order of life. Kunt\'e9
 refused to allow her husband to adopt such life, but at last Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e4\'eb\'f2u gave her permission to become a mother of sons by calling some other suitable personalities. Kunt\'e9
 did not accept this proposal at first, but when vivid examples were set by P\'e4\'eb\'f2u she agreed. Thus by dint of the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 mantra }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 awarded by Durv\'e4s\'e4 }{
\f35\fs28\insrsid16606422\charrsid16606422 Muni}{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592  she called for Dharmar\'e4ja, and thus Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira was born. She called for demigod V\'e4yu (air), and thus Bh\'e9
ma was born. She called for Indra, the King of heaven, and thus Arjuna was born. The other two sons, namely Nakula and Sahadeva, were begotten by P\'e4\'eb\'f2u himself in the womb of M\'e4dr\'e9. Later on, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e4\'eb\'f2u
 died at an early age, for which Kunt\'e9 was so aggrieved that she fainted. Two cowives, namely Kunt\'e9 and M\'e4dr\'e9, decided that Kunt\'e9 should live for the maintenance of the five minor children, the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas, and M\'e4dr\'e9
 should accept the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 sat\'e9 }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 rituals by meeting voluntary death along with her husband. This agreement was endorsed by great sages like \'c7atas\'e5\'ec
ga and others present on the occasion.
\par Later on, when the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas were banished from the kingdom by the intrigues of Duryodhana, Kunt\'e9 followed her sons, and she equally faced all sorts of difficulties during those days, During the forest life one demon girl, Hi\'f2imbi, wanted Bh
\'e9ma as her husband, which was refused by Bh\'e9ma, but when the girl approached Kunt\'e9 and Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira, they ordered Bh\'e9ma to accept her proposal and give her a son. As a result of this combination, Gha\'f6
otkach was born, and he fought very valiantly with his father against the Kauravas. In their forest life they lived with a }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'eba }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
family that was in trouble because of one Bak\'e4sura demon, and Kunt\'e9 ordered Bh\'e9ma to kill the Bak\'e4sura to protect the }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 br\'e4hma\'eba }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 
family against troubles created by the demon. She advised Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira to start for the P\'e4\'efc\'e4la-de\'e7a. Draupad\'e9 was gained in this P\'e4\'efc\'e4la-de\'e7a by Arjuna, but by order of Kunt\'e9 all the five brothers of the P\'e4\'eb\'f2
avas became equally the husbands of P\'e4\'efc\'e4l\'e9 or Draupad\'e9. She was married with five P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas in the presence of Vy\'e4sadeva. Kunt\'e9dev\'e9 never forgot her first child, Kar\'eba, and after Kar\'eba\rquote 
s death in the Battle of Kuruk\'f1etra she lamented and admitted before her other sons that Kar\'eba was her eldest son prior to her marriage with Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e4\'eb\'f2u. After the Battle of Kuruk\'f1etra, when Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a was going back home, her prayers for the Lord are excellently explained. Later she went to the forest with G\'e4ndh\'e4r\'e9
 for severe penance. She used to take meals after each thirty days. She finally sat down in profound meditation and later burned to ashes in a forest fire.
\par }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592      Draupad\'e9: }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 The most chaste daughter of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Drupada and partly an incarnation of goddess \'c7ac\'e9, the wife of Indra. Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Drupada performed a great sacrifice under the superintendence of the sage Yaja. By his first offering, Dh\'e5\'f1\'f6adyumna was born, and by the second offering, Draupad\'e9 was born. She is therefore the sister of Dh\'e5\'f1\'f6adyumna
, and she is also named P\'e4\'efc\'e4l\'e9. The five P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas married her as a common wife, and each of them begot a son in her. Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira begot a son named Pratibindh, Bh\'e9
masena begot a son named Sutasome, Arjuna begot \'c7rutak}{\f35\fs28\insrsid15290236 i}{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 rti, Nakula begot }{\f35\fs28\insrsid15290236 S}{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 at}{\f35\fs28\insrsid15290236 a}{
\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 n}{\f35\fs28\insrsid15290236 i}{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ka, and Sahadeva begot }{\f35\fs28\insrsid15290236 S}{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 rutak}{\f35\fs28\insrsid15290236 a}{
\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ma. She is described as a most beautiful lady, equal to her mother-in-law Kunt\'e9. During her birth there was an aero-message that she should be called K\'e5\'f1\'eb\'e4
. The same message also declared that she is born to kill many a }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 k\'f1atriya. }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 By dint of her blessings from \'c7a\'ec
kara, she was awarded five husbands, equally qualified. When she preferred to select her own husband, princes and kings were invited from all the countries of the world. She was married with the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas during their exile i
n the forest, but when they went back home Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Drupada gave them immense wealth as a dowry. She was well received by all the daughters-in-law of Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6
ra. When she was lost in a gambling game, she was forcibly dragged into the assembly hall, and an attempt was made to see her naked beauty by Du\'f9\'e7\'e4sana, even though there were elderly persons like Bh\'e9\'f1ma and Dro\'eb
a present. She was a great devotee of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and by her praying, the Lord Himself became an unlimited garment to save her from the insult. A demon of the name Jat\'e4sura kidnapped her, but her second husband Bh\'e9
masena killed the demon and saved her. She saved the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas from the curse of Mahar\'f1i Durv\'e4s\'e4 by the grace of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. When the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas lived incognito in the palace of Vir\'e4\'f6}{\f35\fs28\insrsid15290236 a}{
\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 , K\'e9caka was attracted by her exquisite beauty, and by arrangement with Bh\'e9ma the devil was killed and she was saved. She was very much aggrieved when her five sons were killed by A\'e7vatth\'e4m\'e4
. At the last stage, she accompanied her husband Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira and others and fell on the way. The cause of her falling was explained by Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira, but when Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira entered the heavenly planet he saw Draupad\'e9
 gloriously present there as the goddess of fortune in the heavenly planet.
\par }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592      Subhadr\'e4: }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Daughter of Vasudeva and sister of Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. She was not only a very dear daughter of Vasudeva, but also a very dear sister to both K\'e5\'f1\'eba and Baladeva. The two brothers and sister are represented in the famous Jagann\'e4tha Temple of Pur\'e9, and the temple is still visited by
 thousands of pilgrims daily. This temple is in remembrance of the Lord\rquote s visit at Kuruk\'f1etra during an occasion of solar eclipse and His subsequent meeting with the residents of V\'e5nd\'e4vana. The meeting of R\'e4\'f2ha and K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a during this occasion is a very pathetic story, and Lord }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9 }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Caitanya in the ecstasy of R\'e4dh\'e4r\'e4\'eb\'e9 always pined for Lord }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9 }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 K\'e5\'f1\'eba at Jagann\'e4tha Pur\'e9. While Arjuna was at Dv\'e4rak\'e4, he wanted to have Subhadr\'e4
 as his queen, and he expressed his desire to Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9 }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 K\'e5\'f1\'eba knew that His elder
 brother, Lord Baladeva, was arranging her marriage elsewhere, and since He did not dare to go against the arrangement of Baladeva, He advised Arjuna to kidnap Subhadr\'e4
. So when all of them were on a pleasure trip on the Raivata Hill, Arjuna managed to kidnap Subhadr\'e4 according to the plan of }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9 }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 K\'e5\'f1\'eba. }{
\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 \'c7r\'e9 }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 Baladeva was very angry at Arjuna, and He wanted to kill him, but Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba implored His brother to excuse Arjuna. Then Subhadr\'e4
 was duly married with Arjuna, and Abhimanyu was born of Subhadr\'e4. At the premature death of Abhimanyu, Subhadr\'e4 was very mortified, but on the birth of Par\'e9k\'f1it she was happy and solaced.
\par }{\f35\fs28\insrsid15290236 
