\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 i.e., those who are always rapt in the service of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, is significant. The Yadavas and the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas, who were always rapt in the thought of the Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a and His different transcendental activities, were all pure devotees of the Lord like Vidura. Vidura left home in order to devote himself completely to the service of the Lord, but the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas and the Y\'e4
davas were always rapt in the thought of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Thus there is no difference in their pure devotional qualities. Either remaining at home or leaving home, the real qualification of a pure devotee is to become rapt in the thought of K\'e5\'f1
\'eba favorably, }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ie}{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 ., }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 knowing well that Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the Absolute Personality of Godhead. Ka\'e0sa, Jar
\'e4sandha, \'c7i\'e7up\'e4la and other demons like them were also always rapt in the thought of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, but they were absorbed in a different way, namely unfavorably, or thinking Him to be a powerful man only. Therefore, Ka\'e0sa and \'c7i
\'e7up\'e4la are not on the same level of pure devotees like Vidura, the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas or the Y\'e4davas.
\par Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira was also always rapt in the thought of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba and His associates at Dv\'e4rak\'e4. Otherwise he would not have asked all about them from Vidura. Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6
hira is, therefore, on the same level of devotion as Vidura, although engaged in the state affairs of the kingdom of the world.
