Saintly persons like Vidura must be treated as well as a denizen from heaven. In those days denizens of heavenly planets used to visit homes like that of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira, and sometimes persons like Arjuna and others 
used to visit higher planets. N\'e4rada is a spaceman who can travel unrestrictedly, not only within the material universes but also in the spiritual universes. Even N\'e4rada used to visit the palace of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6
hira and what to speak of other celestial demigods. It is only the spiritual culture of the people concerned that makes interplanetary travel possible, even in the present body. Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6
hira therefore received Vidura in the manner of a reception offered to the demigods.
\par Mah\'e4tm\'e4 Vidura had already adopted the renounced order of life, and therefore he did not return to his paternal palace to enjoy some material comforts. He accepted out of his own mercy what was offered to him by Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6
hira, but the purpose of living in the palace was to deliver his too much materially attached elder brother Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6ra. Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6ra lost all his state and descendants in the fight with Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6
hira, and still, due to his sense of helplessness, he did not feel ashamed to accept the charity and hospitality of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira. On the part of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6
hira, it was quite in order to maintain his uncle in a befitting manner, but acceptance of such magnanimous hospitality by Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6ra was not at all desirable. He accepted it because he t
hought that there was no other alternative. Vidura particularly came to enlighten Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6
ra and to give him a lift to the higher status of spiritual cognition. It is the duty of enlightened souls to deliver the fallen ones, and Vidura came for that reason. But talks of spiritual enlightenment are so refreshing that while instructing Dh\'e5tar
\'e4\'f1\'f6ra, Vidura attracted the attention of all the members of the family, and all of them took pleasure in hearing him patiently. This is the way of spiritual realization.
 The message should be heard attentively, and if spoken by a realized soul, it will act on the dormant heart of the conditioned soul. And by continuously hearing, one can attain the perfect stage of self-realization.
