 therefore spiritual instruction, as was given to old Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6ra, was equally applicable to younger Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6
hira. As a matter of fact, everyone in the royal palace including the King and his brothers and mother was raptly attending the lectures. But it was known to Vidura that his instructions were especially meant for Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6
ra, who was too materialistic. The word }{\i\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 r\'e4jan }{\f35\fs28\insrsid2639816\charrsid12326592 is especially addressed to Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6ra significantly. Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6
ra was the eldest son of his father, and therefore according to law he was to be installed on the throne of Hastin\'e4
pura. But because he was blind from birth, he was disqualified from his rightful claim. But he could not forget the bereavement, and his disappointment was somewhat compensated after the death of P\'e4\'eb\'f2u, hi
s younger brother. His younger brother left behind him some minor children, and Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6
ra became the natural guardian of them, but at heart he wanted to become the factual King and hand over the kingdom to his own sons, headed by Duryodhana. With all these imperial ambitions, Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6
ra wanted to become a king and contrive all sorts of intrigues in consultation with his brother-in-law \'c7akuni. But everything failed by the will of the Lord, and at the last stage, even by losing everything, men and money, h
e wanted to remain as King, being the eldest uncle of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira. Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira, as a matter of duty, maintained Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6ra in royal honor, and Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6
ra was happily passing away his numbered days in the illusion of becoming a king or the royal uncle of King Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira. Vidura, as a saint and as the duty-bound affectionate youngest brother of Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6ra, wanted to awaken Dh\'e5tar
\'e4\'f1\'f6ra from his slumber of disease and old age. Vidura therefore sarcastically addressed Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6ra as the \'93King,\'94
 which he was actually not. Everyone is the servant of eternal time, and therefore no one can be king in this material order. King means the person who can order. The celebrated English King wanted to order time and tide, but the time and tide refused 
to obey his order. Therefore one is a false king in the material world, and Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6
ra was particularly reminded of this false position and of the factual fearful happenings which had already approached him at that time. Vidura asked him to get out immedi
ately, if he wanted to be saved from the fearful situation which was approaching him fast. He did not ask Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira in that way because he knew that a king like Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6
hira is aware of all the fearful situations of this flimsy world, and he would take care of himself, in due course, even though Vidura might not be present at that time.
